WEBVTT

1
00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.620
What is the most resilient parasite?

2
00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.640
Bacteria?

3
00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.460
A virus?

4
00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:54.900
An intestinal worm?

5
00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.220
What Mr. Cobb is trying to say.

6
00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.960
An idea.

7
00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.560
Resilient, highly contagious.

8
00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.600
Once an idea has taken hold of the brain,

9
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.000
it's almost impossible to eradicate.

10
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.640
An idea that is fully formed, fully understood,

11
00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.480
that sticks.

12
00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.720
Right in there somewhere.

13
00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.720
For someone like you to steal?

14
00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.000
Yes, in the dream state,

15
00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.640
your conscious defenses are lowered

16
00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.400
and it makes your thoughts vulnerable to theft.

17
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.880
It's called extraction.

18
00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.480
So, Saito, we can train your subconscious

19
00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.480
to defend itself from even the most skilled extractor.

20
00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:30.720
How can I do that?

21
00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.890
Because I am the most skilled extractor.

22
00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.410
I know how to search your mind and find your secrets.

23
00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.530
I know the tricks, and I can teach them to you

24
00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.270
so that even when you're asleep,

25
00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:42.650
your defense is never down.

26
00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:45.830
Look, if you want my help,

27
00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.610
you're gonna have to be completely open with me.

28
00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.370
I need to know my way around your thoughts

29
00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.690
better than your wife,

30
00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.050
better than your therapist, better than anyone.

31
00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.490
If this is a dream and you have a safe full of secrets,

32
00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:59.290
I need to know what's in that safe.

33
00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.770
In order for this all to work,

34
00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:05.780
you need to completely let me in.

35
00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.700
Enjoy your evening, gentlemen.

36
00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.540
As I consider your proposal.

37
00:04:09.540 --> 00:05:19.820
Fino's in the safe.

38
00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:23.700
He looked right at it when I mentioned secrets.

39
00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.750
What's he doing now?

40
00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.030
He's heading back to the room.

41
00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.230
All right, I'll take care of this.

42
00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:31.190
Okay, make sure you do.

43
00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:40.990
We're here to work.

44
00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:48.060
If I turn, would I survive?

45
00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.620
A clean dive, perhaps.

46
00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.180
Ma, what are you doing here?

47
00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.940
I thought you might be missing me.

48
00:05:54.980 --> 00:06:00.730
Not that I am.

49
00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:03.660
So what?

50
00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.060
Looks like you're off his taste.

51
00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.740
Actually, the subject is partial

52
00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.340
to post-war British painters.

53
00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:22.690
Please, have a seat.

54
00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:34.430
Did the children miss me?

55
00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:35.670
What are you doing?

56
00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.670
Just getting some fresh air.

57
00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.150
Stay where you are, Ma.

58
00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:24.860
Have an envelope, Mr. Cobb.

59
00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.740
Did she tell you?

60
00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.740
Have you known all along?

61
00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.380
Are you here to steal from me,

62
00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:37.450
or that we are actually asleep?

63
00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:44.100
I want to know the name of your employee.

64
00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:46.340
I'm in a dream, my Ma.

65
00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.380
That depends on what you're threatening.

66
00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:51.380
Killing him would just wake him up.

67
00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:58.790
But pain is in the mind.

68
00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:01.670
And judging by the decor,

69
00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:16.490
we're in your mind, aren't we, Arthur?

70
00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:17.330
Put your shield!

71
00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:18.170
I know.

72
00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:19.210
Dreams collapse.

73
00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:21.770
Try to keep Sator Wonder a little bit longer.

74
00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:22.770
We're almost there.

75
00:09:22.770 --> 00:10:24.030
No work, wake him up.

76
00:10:24.030 --> 00:11:50.680
My head on security knows this about me.

77
00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:51.800
How did he find it?

78
00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.680
It's very difficult for a man of your position

79
00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.560
to keep a love nest like this secret,

80
00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:59.000
particularly where there's a married woman involved.

81
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.000
It's you and them.

82
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.200
Yet, here we are.

83
00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:03.200
For the dilemma.

84
00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.520
They're getting closer.

85
00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:05.920
You got what you came for.

86
00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.560
Well, that's not true.

87
00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.320
You left out a key piece of information, didn't you?

88
00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.160
You held something back

89
00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.720
because you knew what we were up to.

90
00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.680
The question is, why'd you let us in at all?

91
00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:16.520
An audition.

92
00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:18.640
An audition for what?

93
00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:19.720
It doesn't matter.

94
00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.040
You failed.

95
00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:24.000
We extracted every bit of information you had in there.

96
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.800
But your deception was obvious.

97
00:13:16.500 --> 00:14:01.260
It won't last two days.

98
00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:12.360
The reputation of Mr. Carter.

99
00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.280
How'd it go?

100
00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:14.120
Not good.

101
00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:24.930
It ain't a dream, huh?

102
00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:28.690
But in my dream, you play by my rules.

103
00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:30.970
Ah, yes, but you see, Mr. Sator,

104
00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.370
we're not in your dream.

105
00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:33.210
We're in mine.

106
00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:34.450
Asshole.

107
00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:45.050
How'd he mess up the carpet?

108
00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.250
It wasn't my fault.

109
00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.570
You're the architect.

110
00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:49.610
I didn't know he was gonna rub his damn cheek on it.

111
00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:50.450
That's enough.

112
00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.450
You, what the hell was all that?

113
00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.690
I have it under control.

114
00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.370
I'd hate to see you out of control.

115
00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.570
We don't have time for this.

116
00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:01.370
I'm getting off at Kyoto.

117
00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:03.410
Why, he's not gonna check every compartment?

118
00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:04.970
Well, I don't like trains.

119
00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.610
Listen, every man for himself.

120
00:15:07.610 --> 00:16:23.220
Yes, hello?

121
00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:28.300
Hey, guys, hey.

122
00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.140
How are you, how you doing?

123
00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:34.140
Okay.

124
00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:36.260
It was just okay.

125
00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.460
Is that you, Jane?

126
00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:44.100
I can't, sweetheart, I can't.

127
00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:46.980
It's not for a while, remember?

128
00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:53.770
I told you I'm away because I'm working, right?

129
00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:59.510
Phillipa, is that you?

130
00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:03.300
Put grandma on the phone for me, will you?

131
00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:09.440
Well, I just hope she's wrong about that.

132
00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:19.890
Yeah, Jane, not this.

133
00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:23.820
Mommy's not here anymore.

134
00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:34.000
Listen, I'm gonna send some presents with grandpa, all right?

135
00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.600
And you be good.

136
00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:46.650
Our rod's on the roof.

137
00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:55.460
Right.

138
00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:57.100
Hey, are you okay?

139
00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:58.580
Yeah, I'm fine, why?

140
00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:01.460
Well, down in the dream, I'm all showing up.

141
00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:02.300
Welcome, Mom.

142
00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:04.580
Sorry about your leg, it won't happen again.

143
00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:05.740
It's getting worse, isn't it?

144
00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:08.380
One apology's all you're getting, all right, Arthur?

145
00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:09.220
Wasn't that you?

146
00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:11.140
He hasn't shown, you wanna wait?

147
00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:13.540
No, we're supposed to deliver Saito's expansion plans

148
00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.180
to Cobol Engineering two hours ago.

149
00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:17.060
By now they know we failed.

150
00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:18.420
It's time we disappeared.

151
00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:20.820
Where you gonna go?

152
00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:21.980
Bueno, saris.

153
00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.980
I can lie low there, maybe sniff out a job

154
00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:25.820
and things quiet down.

155
00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:26.660
You?

156
00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:27.860
Stay tight.

157
00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:35.700
Send my regards.

158
00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:37.820
He saw the art, thought to come to me

159
00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:41.060
and bargain for his life.

160
00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:47.110
So, I offer you the satisfaction.

161
00:18:47.110 --> 00:19:01.720
It's not the way I deal with things.

162
00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.560
What will you do with it?

163
00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:07.800
Nothing, but I can't speak for Cobol Engineering.

164
00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:24.440
What do you want from us?

165
00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:29.290
Inception.

166
00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.610
If you can steal an idea from someone's mind,

167
00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:33.650
why can't you plan one day instead?

168
00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:36.010
Okay, here's me planning an idea in your head.

169
00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:38.290
I say to you, don't think about elephants.

170
00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:39.770
What are you thinking about?

171
00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:40.610
Elephants.

172
00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:42.050
Right, but it's not your idea

173
00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:44.050
because you know I gave it to you.

174
00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:45.810
The subject's mind can always trace

175
00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:47.170
the genesis of the idea.

176
00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:49.010
True inspiration's impossible to fake.

177
00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:53.910
It's not true.

178
00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:55.430
Are you offering me a choice?

179
00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:57.550
Because I can find my own way

180
00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:58.950
to squirt things with Cobol.

181
00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:01.230
Then you do have a choice.

182
00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:08.140
And I choose to leave, sir.

183
00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:15.020
Tell the crew where you want to go.

184
00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:20.520
Hey, Mr. Cobb, how would you like to go home?

185
00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:22.760
To America?

186
00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:24.680
To your children?

187
00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:27.720
Can't fix that.

188
00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.320
No one can.

189
00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:30.920
Just like Inception.

190
00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:36.300
Cobb, come on.

191
00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:37.980
How complex is the idea?

192
00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:39.220
Simple enough.

193
00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:40.620
No idea is simple

194
00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:43.300
when you need to plant it in somebody else's mind.

195
00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:46.980
My main competitor is an old man in poor health.

196
00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:50.060
His son will soon inherit control of the corporation.

197
00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.980
I need him to decide to break up his father's empire.

198
00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.340
Cobb, we should walk away from this.

199
00:20:57.340 --> 00:21:00.660
Hold on.

200
00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.180
If I were to do this,

201
00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:04.020
if I even could do it,

202
00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:06.180
I'd need a guarantee.

203
00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:07.820
How do I know you can deliver?

204
00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:08.660
You don't.

205
00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:10.900
But I can.

206
00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:12.820
So,

207
00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:15.820
do you want to take a leap of faith

208
00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:18.300
or become an old man

209
00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:26.760
filled with regret, waiting to die alone?

210
00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.800
Assemble your team, Mr. Cobb,

211
00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:39.500
and choose your people more wisely.

212
00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:43.910
Look, I know how much you want to go home.

213
00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:44.910
This can't be done.

214
00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:46.670
Yes, it can.

215
00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:49.070
I just have to go deep enough.

216
00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:52.060
You don't know that.

217
00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:55.260
I've done it before.

218
00:21:55.260 --> 00:22:01.940
What would you do it to?

219
00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:05.400
Go on to Paris.

220
00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:23.700
We're gonna need a new architect.

221
00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:27.670
You never did like your office, did you?

222
00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:32.460
No space to think in that broom cupboard.

223
00:22:32.460 --> 00:22:36.140
Is it safe for you to be here?

224
00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:38.380
Extradition between France and the United States

225
00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:40.460
is a bureaucratic nightmare, you know that?

226
00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:41.620
I think they might find a way

227
00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:43.420
to make it work in your case.

228
00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:47.580
Look, I brought these for you to give to the kids

229
00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:48.620
when you have a chance.

230
00:22:48.620 --> 00:22:51.180
It'll take more than the occasional stuffed animal

231
00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:54.380
to convince those children they still have a father.

232
00:22:54.380 --> 00:22:55.380
I'm just doing what I know.

233
00:22:55.380 --> 00:22:57.540
I'm doing what you taught me.

234
00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:59.140
I never taught you to be a thief.

235
00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:01.460
No, you taught me to navigate people's minds,

236
00:23:01.460 --> 00:23:02.980
but after what happened,

237
00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:04.660
there weren't a whole lot of legitimate ways

238
00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:11.660
for me to use that skill.

239
00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:15.300
What are you doing here, Doug?

240
00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:16.980
I think I found a way home.

241
00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:21.580
It's a job for some very, very powerful people,

242
00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:25.660
people who I believe can fix my charges permanently.

243
00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:28.780
But I need your help.

244
00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:32.100
You're here to corrupt one of my brightest and best.

245
00:23:32.100 --> 00:23:33.140
You know what I'm offering?

246
00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.180
You have to let them decide for themselves.

247
00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:36.020
Money?

248
00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:38.540
Not just money, you remember.

249
00:23:38.540 --> 00:23:41.980
It's the chance to build cathedrals, entire cities,

250
00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:43.620
things that never existed,

251
00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:47.060
things that couldn't exist in the real world.

252
00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:49.580
So you want me to let someone else

253
00:23:50.420 --> 00:23:52.380
follow you into your fantasy?

254
00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:53.980
They don't actually come into the dream.

255
00:23:53.980 --> 00:23:55.980
They just design the levels

256
00:23:55.980 --> 00:23:58.100
and teach them to the dreamers, that's all.

257
00:23:58.100 --> 00:24:02.020
Design it yourself.

258
00:24:02.020 --> 00:24:16.140
Ma won't let me.

259
00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:18.900
Those kids, your grandchildren,

260
00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:21.060
they're waiting for their father to come back home.

261
00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:22.740
That's their reality.

262
00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:26.780
And this job, this last job, that's how I get there.

263
00:24:26.780 --> 00:24:30.500
I would not be standing here if I knew any other way.

264
00:24:30.500 --> 00:24:40.770
Hector was as good as I was.

265
00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:42.130
I've got somebody better.

266
00:24:43.010 --> 00:24:48.360
Ariadne, I'd like you to meet Mr. Cobb.

267
00:24:49.520 --> 00:24:50.760
Pleased to meet you.

268
00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:51.840
If you have a few moments,

269
00:24:51.840 --> 00:24:55.800
Mr. Cobb has a job offer he'd like to discuss with you.

270
00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:57.040
A work place, sir?

271
00:24:57.040 --> 00:24:58.600
Not exactly.

272
00:24:58.600 --> 00:25:00.680
I have a test for you.

273
00:25:00.680 --> 00:25:02.840
You're not gonna tell me anything about this script?

274
00:25:02.840 --> 00:25:04.200
Before I describe the job,

275
00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:05.680
I have to know you can do it.

276
00:25:05.680 --> 00:25:06.560
Why?

277
00:25:06.560 --> 00:25:11.860
It's not, strictly speaking, legal.

278
00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:14.740
You have two minutes to design a maze

279
00:25:14.740 --> 00:25:18.420
that it takes one minute to solve.

280
00:25:18.420 --> 00:25:21.860
Stop.

281
00:25:21.860 --> 00:25:29.960
Again, stop.

282
00:25:29.960 --> 00:26:06.830
It's gonna have to be better than that.

283
00:26:06.830 --> 00:26:09.470
We only use a fraction of our brain's true potential.

284
00:26:09.470 --> 00:26:11.550
Now, that's when we're awake.

285
00:26:11.550 --> 00:26:14.470
When we're asleep, our mind can do almost anything.

286
00:26:14.470 --> 00:26:15.750
Such as?

287
00:26:15.750 --> 00:26:17.550
Well, imagine you're designing a building, right?

288
00:26:17.550 --> 00:26:19.830
You consciously create each aspect.

289
00:26:19.830 --> 00:26:22.470
But sometimes it feels like it's almost creating itself,

290
00:26:22.470 --> 00:26:23.310
if you know what I mean.

291
00:26:23.310 --> 00:26:25.870
Yeah, yeah, like I'm discovering it.

292
00:26:25.870 --> 00:26:28.430
Genuine inspiration, right?

293
00:26:28.430 --> 00:26:31.950
Now, in a dream, our mind continuously does this.

294
00:26:31.950 --> 00:26:36.950
We create and perceive our world simultaneously,

295
00:26:36.990 --> 00:26:38.390
and our mind does this so well

296
00:26:38.390 --> 00:26:40.510
that we don't even know what's happening.

297
00:26:40.510 --> 00:26:43.710
That allows us to get right in the middle of that process.

298
00:26:43.710 --> 00:26:44.550
How?

299
00:26:44.550 --> 00:26:45.790
By taking over the creating part.

300
00:26:45.790 --> 00:26:47.390
Now, this is where I need you.

301
00:26:47.390 --> 00:26:50.030
You create the world of the dream.

302
00:26:50.030 --> 00:26:52.630
We bring the subject into that dream,

303
00:26:52.630 --> 00:26:55.350
and they fill it with their subconscious.

304
00:26:55.350 --> 00:26:58.630
How could I ever acquire enough detail

305
00:26:58.630 --> 00:27:00.550
to make them think that it's reality?

306
00:27:00.550 --> 00:27:04.310
Well, dreams, they feel real while we're in them, right?

307
00:27:04.310 --> 00:27:05.430
It's only when we wake up

308
00:27:05.430 --> 00:27:08.070
that we realize something was actually strange.

309
00:27:09.270 --> 00:27:10.230
Let me ask you a question.

310
00:27:10.230 --> 00:27:13.870
You never really remember the beginning of a dream,

311
00:27:13.870 --> 00:27:14.710
do you?

312
00:27:14.710 --> 00:27:17.670
You always wind up right in the middle of what's going on.

313
00:27:17.670 --> 00:27:18.870
I guess, yeah.

314
00:27:18.870 --> 00:27:20.830
So how did we end up here?

315
00:27:20.830 --> 00:27:23.150
Well, we just came from the, uh...

316
00:27:23.150 --> 00:27:24.430
Think about it, Ariadne.

317
00:27:24.430 --> 00:27:25.950
How did you get here?

318
00:27:26.990 --> 00:27:32.420
Where are you right now?

319
00:27:32.420 --> 00:27:33.300
We're dreaming?

320
00:27:33.300 --> 00:27:35.580
You're actually in the middle of the workshop right now,

321
00:27:35.580 --> 00:27:36.420
sleeping.

322
00:27:36.420 --> 00:27:38.580
This is your first lesson in shared dreaming.

323
00:27:38.580 --> 00:27:39.420
Stay calm.

324
00:27:40.460 --> 00:28:21.710
It's never just a dream, is it?

325
00:28:21.710 --> 00:28:23.390
A face full of glass hurts like hell.

326
00:28:23.390 --> 00:28:25.790
When you're in it, it feels real.

327
00:28:25.790 --> 00:28:27.670
That's why the military developed dream sharing.

328
00:28:27.670 --> 00:28:30.150
It was a training program for soldiers to shoot

329
00:28:30.150 --> 00:28:33.390
and stab and strangle each other and then wake up.

330
00:28:33.390 --> 00:28:35.390
How did architects become involved?

331
00:28:35.430 --> 00:28:39.150
Someone had to design the dreams, right?

332
00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:41.510
Why don't you give us another five minutes?

333
00:28:41.510 --> 00:28:42.630
Five minutes?

334
00:28:43.550 --> 00:28:44.430
What?

335
00:28:44.430 --> 00:28:46.670
We were talking for, like, at least an hour.

336
00:28:46.670 --> 00:28:48.910
In a dream, your mind functions more quickly.

337
00:28:48.910 --> 00:28:52.070
Therefore, time seems to feel more slow.

338
00:28:52.070 --> 00:28:53.390
Five minutes in the real world

339
00:28:53.390 --> 00:28:55.030
gives you an hour in the dream?

340
00:28:56.190 --> 00:28:57.550
Why don't you see what you can get up to

341
00:28:57.550 --> 00:29:05.290
in five minutes?

342
00:29:05.290 --> 00:29:06.650
The basic layout.

343
00:29:06.650 --> 00:29:10.250
Bookstore, cafe, almost everything else is here, too.

344
00:29:10.250 --> 00:29:11.210
Who are the people?

345
00:29:11.250 --> 00:29:13.250
The projections of my subconscious.

346
00:29:13.250 --> 00:29:14.090
Yours?

347
00:29:14.090 --> 00:29:14.930
Yes.

348
00:29:14.930 --> 00:29:15.850
Remember, you are the dreamer.

349
00:29:15.850 --> 00:29:17.170
You build this world.

350
00:29:17.170 --> 00:29:18.290
I am the subject.

351
00:29:18.290 --> 00:29:20.050
My mind populates it.

352
00:29:20.050 --> 00:29:22.250
You can literally talk to my subconscious.

353
00:29:22.250 --> 00:29:24.170
That's one of the ways we extract information

354
00:29:24.170 --> 00:29:25.010
from the subject.

355
00:29:25.010 --> 00:29:26.610
How else do you do it?

356
00:29:26.610 --> 00:29:30.730
By creating something secure like a bank vault or a jail.

357
00:29:30.730 --> 00:29:33.130
The mind automatically fills it with information

358
00:29:33.130 --> 00:29:35.810
it's trying to protect, understand?

359
00:29:35.810 --> 00:29:37.810
Then you break in and steal it.

360
00:29:37.810 --> 00:29:38.850
Well.

361
00:29:38.850 --> 00:29:40.330
I guess I thought that

362
00:29:40.370 --> 00:29:42.490
the dream space would be all about the visual,

363
00:29:42.490 --> 00:29:44.690
but it's more about the feel of it.

364
00:29:45.650 --> 00:29:46.490
My question is,

365
00:29:46.490 --> 00:29:47.930
what happens when you start messing

366
00:29:47.930 --> 00:29:49.250
with the physics of it all?

367
00:29:49.250 --> 00:31:04.720
Feels that someone else is creating this world.

368
00:31:04.720 --> 00:31:06.160
The more you change things,

369
00:31:06.160 --> 00:31:09.120
the quicker the projections start to converge on you.

370
00:31:09.120 --> 00:31:10.160
Converge?

371
00:31:10.160 --> 00:31:12.440
They sense the foreign nature of the dreamer.

372
00:31:12.440 --> 00:31:15.640
They attack like white blood cells fighting an infection.

373
00:31:15.640 --> 00:31:16.960
Like they're gonna attack us?

374
00:31:16.960 --> 00:31:25.320
No.

375
00:31:25.320 --> 00:31:26.160
But I'm telling you,

376
00:31:26.160 --> 00:31:28.080
if you keep changing things like this.

377
00:31:33.100 --> 00:31:35.220
Telling your subconscious to take it easy?

378
00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:36.460
My subconscious.

379
00:31:36.460 --> 00:32:47.050
Remember, I can't control it.

380
00:32:47.050 --> 00:32:50.780
Place is real, isn't it?

381
00:32:50.780 --> 00:32:52.780
Never recreate places from your memory.

382
00:32:52.780 --> 00:32:54.300
Always imagine new places.

383
00:32:54.300 --> 00:32:56.260
Well, you gotta draw from stuff you know, right?

384
00:32:56.260 --> 00:32:57.340
Only use details.

385
00:32:57.340 --> 00:32:59.460
A street lamp or a phone booth.

386
00:32:59.460 --> 00:33:00.620
Never entire areas.

387
00:33:00.620 --> 00:33:01.620
Why not?

388
00:33:01.620 --> 00:33:03.100
Because building a dream from your memory

389
00:33:03.100 --> 00:33:04.780
is the easiest way to lose your grasp

390
00:33:04.780 --> 00:33:06.620
on what's real and what is a dream.

391
00:33:06.620 --> 00:33:07.820
Is that what happened to you?

392
00:33:07.820 --> 00:33:10.740
Listen, this has nothing to do with me, understand?

393
00:33:10.740 --> 00:33:13.660
Is that why you need me to build your dreams?

394
00:33:13.660 --> 00:33:14.620
Get off of me.

395
00:33:14.620 --> 00:33:15.460
Back up.

396
00:33:15.460 --> 00:33:16.300
Back up!

397
00:33:16.500 --> 00:33:17.340
Get off of me!

398
00:33:17.340 --> 00:33:18.180
Come!

399
00:33:18.180 --> 00:33:19.020
Wake me up!

400
00:33:19.020 --> 00:33:20.140
Wake me up!

401
00:33:20.140 --> 00:33:21.260
Come!

402
00:33:21.260 --> 00:33:29.680
Wake me up!

403
00:33:29.680 --> 00:33:30.520
You're okay.

404
00:33:30.520 --> 00:33:31.720
You're okay.

405
00:33:31.720 --> 00:33:32.560
Hey.

406
00:33:32.560 --> 00:33:33.400
Why?

407
00:33:33.400 --> 00:33:35.480
Why wouldn't I wake up?

408
00:33:35.480 --> 00:33:37.120
Because there was still some time on the clock

409
00:33:37.120 --> 00:33:38.480
and you can't wake up from within the dream

410
00:33:38.480 --> 00:33:39.520
unless you die.

411
00:33:39.520 --> 00:33:40.520
She'll need a totem.

412
00:33:40.520 --> 00:33:41.520
What?

413
00:33:41.520 --> 00:33:42.360
A totem.

414
00:33:42.360 --> 00:33:43.200
It's a small person.

415
00:33:43.200 --> 00:33:45.840
That's some subconscious you've got on you, Cobb.

416
00:33:45.840 --> 00:33:47.080
She's a real charmer.

417
00:33:47.080 --> 00:33:49.400
Oh, I see you met Mrs. Cobb.

418
00:33:49.400 --> 00:33:50.640
She's his wife?

419
00:33:50.640 --> 00:33:52.520
Yeah, so a totem.

420
00:33:52.560 --> 00:33:54.680
You need a small object to potentially have you

421
00:33:54.680 --> 00:33:56.440
something you can have on you all the time

422
00:33:56.440 --> 00:33:57.280
that no one else knows.

423
00:33:57.280 --> 00:33:58.120
Like a coin?

424
00:33:58.120 --> 00:34:00.760
No, it needs to be more unique than that.

425
00:34:00.760 --> 00:34:05.310
This is a loaded die.

426
00:34:05.310 --> 00:34:06.150
I can't let you touch it.

427
00:34:06.150 --> 00:34:07.190
That would defeat the purpose.

428
00:34:07.190 --> 00:34:09.230
The only I know the balance and the weight

429
00:34:09.230 --> 00:34:11.950
of this particular loaded die.

430
00:34:11.950 --> 00:34:13.630
That way, when you look at your totem,

431
00:34:13.630 --> 00:34:14.550
you know beyond a doubt

432
00:34:14.550 --> 00:34:20.390
that you're not in someone else's dream.

433
00:34:20.390 --> 00:34:23.150
I don't know if you can't see what's going on

434
00:34:23.150 --> 00:34:24.870
or if you just don't want to,

435
00:34:24.870 --> 00:34:26.750
but Cobb has some serious problems

436
00:34:26.750 --> 00:34:28.430
that he's tried to bury down there,

437
00:34:28.430 --> 00:34:31.230
and I'm not about to just open my mind

438
00:34:31.230 --> 00:34:38.390
to someone like that.

439
00:34:38.390 --> 00:34:39.830
She'll be back.

440
00:34:39.830 --> 00:34:42.510
I've never seen anyone pick it up that quickly before.

441
00:34:42.510 --> 00:34:44.470
Reality's not gonna be enough for her now,

442
00:34:44.470 --> 00:34:47.550
and when she comes back,

443
00:34:47.550 --> 00:34:48.390
when she comes back,

444
00:34:48.390 --> 00:34:50.230
you're gonna have her building mazes.

445
00:34:50.230 --> 00:34:51.070
Where are you gonna be?

446
00:34:51.070 --> 00:34:52.630
I gotta go visit Eames.

447
00:34:52.630 --> 00:34:53.790
Eames?

448
00:34:53.790 --> 00:34:54.990
No, he's in Mombasa.

449
00:34:54.990 --> 00:34:56.110
It's Cobalt's backyard.

450
00:34:56.110 --> 00:34:57.870
It's a necessary risk.

451
00:34:57.870 --> 00:34:59.270
There's plenty of good thieves.

452
00:34:59.270 --> 00:35:00.830
We don't just need a thief.

453
00:35:01.830 --> 00:35:03.270
We need a forger.

454
00:35:12.010 --> 00:35:13.490
You can rub them together all you want.

455
00:35:13.490 --> 00:35:15.330
They're not gonna breed.

456
00:35:15.330 --> 00:35:16.170
You never know.

457
00:35:17.290 --> 00:35:18.530
Let me get you a drink.

458
00:35:21.330 --> 00:35:29.340
You'll buy.

459
00:35:29.340 --> 00:35:30.700
Your spelling hasn't improved.

460
00:35:30.700 --> 00:35:31.700
Yes, sir.

461
00:35:31.700 --> 00:35:33.700
How's your handwriting?

462
00:35:33.700 --> 00:35:34.860
It's versatile.

463
00:35:34.860 --> 00:35:35.700
Good.

464
00:35:35.700 --> 00:35:37.580
Thank you very much.

465
00:35:37.580 --> 00:35:38.420
Inception.

466
00:35:39.300 --> 00:35:42.260
Now, before you bother telling me it's impossible.

467
00:35:42.260 --> 00:35:43.620
No, it's perfectly possible.

468
00:35:43.620 --> 00:35:45.820
It's just bloody difficult.

469
00:35:45.820 --> 00:35:47.100
Interesting.

470
00:35:47.100 --> 00:35:50.060
Arthur keeps telling me it can't be done.

471
00:35:50.060 --> 00:35:52.460
Arthur, are you still working with that stick in the mind?

472
00:35:52.460 --> 00:35:54.300
He is good at what he does, right?

473
00:35:54.300 --> 00:35:55.220
Oh, he's the best.

474
00:35:55.220 --> 00:35:56.780
He has no imagination.

475
00:35:56.780 --> 00:35:57.620
Not like you.

476
00:35:57.620 --> 00:35:59.220
Listen, if you're gonna perform Inception,

477
00:35:59.220 --> 00:36:00.820
you need imagination.

478
00:36:00.820 --> 00:36:02.220
Let me ask you something.

479
00:36:03.300 --> 00:36:04.780
Have you done it before?

480
00:36:04.780 --> 00:36:06.020
We tried it.

481
00:36:06.020 --> 00:36:07.380
We got the idea in place,

482
00:36:07.380 --> 00:36:08.540
but it didn't take.

483
00:36:08.540 --> 00:36:10.020
You didn't plant it deep enough?

484
00:36:10.020 --> 00:36:12.340
No, it's not just about depth.

485
00:36:12.380 --> 00:36:14.220
You need the simplest version of the idea

486
00:36:14.220 --> 00:36:16.580
in order for it to grow naturally in your subject's mind.

487
00:36:16.580 --> 00:36:18.140
It's a very subtle art.

488
00:36:18.140 --> 00:36:20.780
So what is this idea that you need to blow?

489
00:36:20.780 --> 00:36:23.100
We need the air of a major corporation

490
00:36:23.100 --> 00:36:25.220
to dissolve his father's empire.

491
00:36:25.220 --> 00:36:26.060
Well, you see, right there,

492
00:36:26.060 --> 00:36:27.540
you have various political motivations

493
00:36:27.540 --> 00:36:29.540
and anti-monopolistic sentiments and so forth,

494
00:36:29.540 --> 00:36:32.820
but all of that stuff, it's really at the mercy

495
00:36:32.820 --> 00:36:34.980
of your subject's prejudice, you see?

496
00:36:34.980 --> 00:36:37.540
And what you have to do is start at the absolute basic.

497
00:36:37.540 --> 00:36:38.460
Which is what?

498
00:36:39.740 --> 00:36:43.820
The relationship with the father.

499
00:36:43.860 --> 00:36:44.820
Do you have a chemist?

500
00:36:44.820 --> 00:36:45.660
No, not yet.

501
00:36:45.660 --> 00:36:46.500
Right, okay.

502
00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:50.100
Well, there's a man here, Yusef Pio.

503
00:36:50.100 --> 00:36:52.780
He formulates his own versions of the compounds.

504
00:36:52.780 --> 00:36:53.860
Why don't you take me there?

505
00:36:53.860 --> 00:36:55.300
Once you've lost your tail.

506
00:36:56.380 --> 00:36:57.540
Man at the bar.

507
00:36:57.540 --> 00:36:58.700
Cobalt Engineering.

508
00:36:58.700 --> 00:37:01.460
That price on my head, was that dead or alive?

509
00:37:01.460 --> 00:37:02.420
Don't remember.

510
00:37:02.420 --> 00:37:04.020
See if he starts shooting.

511
00:37:04.020 --> 00:37:06.220
Run interference, I'll meet you downstairs in the bar

512
00:37:06.220 --> 00:37:07.860
and say half an hour?

513
00:37:07.860 --> 00:37:08.700
Well, back here.

514
00:37:08.700 --> 00:37:10.020
He's the last place they'd suspect.

515
00:37:10.020 --> 00:37:14.830
Mm-hmm, well.

516
00:37:14.830 --> 00:37:16.990
Freddy, Freddy Simmons.

517
00:37:16.990 --> 00:37:20.300
My God, it's you, isn't it?

518
00:37:20.300 --> 00:37:21.140
No.

519
00:37:22.060 --> 00:37:23.540
No, it isn't.

520
00:37:23.540 --> 00:37:24.740
You're not dreaming now, are you?

521
00:37:24.740 --> 00:37:25.580
Oh.

522
00:38:04.420 --> 00:38:05.260
Ah, cafe.

523
00:38:11.650 --> 00:38:12.490
Shh.

524
00:38:20.970 --> 00:38:21.810
Cafe.

525
00:38:25.570 --> 00:38:26.410
Oh.

526
00:38:28.410 --> 00:39:21.550
Mr. Cobb.

527
00:39:21.550 --> 00:39:27.570
I need to protect my investments.

528
00:39:27.570 --> 00:39:29.530
So this is your idea of losing a tail, huh?

529
00:39:29.530 --> 00:39:39.390
Different tail.

530
00:39:39.390 --> 00:39:40.710
Cobb said you'd be back.

531
00:39:42.190 --> 00:39:44.190
I tried not to come, but.

532
00:39:44.190 --> 00:39:45.910
But there's nothing quite like it.

533
00:39:45.910 --> 00:39:50.640
It's just pure creation.

534
00:39:50.640 --> 00:39:53.600
Shall we take a look at some paradoxical architecture?

535
00:39:53.600 --> 00:39:55.040
You're gonna have to master a few tricks

536
00:39:55.040 --> 00:39:57.480
if you're gonna build three complete dream levels.

537
00:39:57.480 --> 00:39:58.320
Excuse me.

538
00:39:59.200 --> 00:40:00.960
What kind of tricks?

539
00:40:01.560 --> 00:40:02.720
In a dream you can cheat architecture

540
00:40:02.720 --> 00:40:04.320
into impossible shapes.

541
00:40:04.320 --> 00:40:06.680
That lets you create closed loops,

542
00:40:06.680 --> 00:40:11.120
like the Penrose steps, the infinite staircase.

543
00:40:21.100 --> 00:40:22.860
A closed loop like that will help you

544
00:40:22.860 --> 00:40:25.260
disguise the boundaries of the dream you create.

545
00:40:25.260 --> 00:40:27.940
But how big do these levels have to be?

546
00:40:27.940 --> 00:40:29.700
Well, it can be anything from the floor of a building

547
00:40:29.700 --> 00:40:31.180
to an entire city,

548
00:40:31.180 --> 00:40:33.220
but they have to be complicated enough

549
00:40:33.220 --> 00:40:34.620
that we can hide from the projections.

550
00:40:34.620 --> 00:40:35.460
A maze.

551
00:40:35.460 --> 00:40:36.300
Right, a maze.

552
00:40:36.300 --> 00:40:37.620
And the better the maze.

553
00:40:37.620 --> 00:40:38.580
Then the longer we have

554
00:40:38.580 --> 00:40:40.580
before the projections catch us.

555
00:40:40.620 --> 00:40:41.460
Zack.

556
00:40:42.580 --> 00:40:44.620
My subconscious seems polite enough.

557
00:40:44.620 --> 00:40:46.340
Wait, it'll turn ugly.

558
00:40:46.340 --> 00:40:47.340
No one likes to feel someone else

559
00:40:47.340 --> 00:40:49.380
messing around in their mind.

560
00:40:49.380 --> 00:40:53.650
Cobb can't build anymore, can he?

561
00:40:53.650 --> 00:40:55.850
I don't know if he can't, but he won't.

562
00:40:55.850 --> 00:40:58.050
He thinks it's safer if he doesn't know the layouts.

563
00:40:58.050 --> 00:40:58.890
Why?

564
00:40:58.890 --> 00:41:00.650
He won't tell me.

565
00:41:00.650 --> 00:41:02.130
I think it's Mal.

566
00:41:02.130 --> 00:41:03.410
Zack's wife?

567
00:41:03.410 --> 00:41:04.610
No, not Zack's.

568
00:41:04.610 --> 00:41:06.130
They're still together?

569
00:41:06.130 --> 00:41:12.180
No, she's dead.

570
00:41:12.180 --> 00:41:18.630
What you see in there is just his projection of her.

571
00:41:18.630 --> 00:41:20.790
What was she like in real life?

572
00:41:20.790 --> 00:41:25.920
She was lovely.

573
00:41:25.920 --> 00:41:27.640
You are seeking a chemist.

574
00:41:27.640 --> 00:41:28.680
Yes.

575
00:41:28.680 --> 00:41:30.360
To formulate compounds for a job.

576
00:41:31.320 --> 00:41:33.320
And to go into the field with us.

577
00:41:33.320 --> 00:41:35.480
No, I rarely go into the field, Mr. Cobb.

578
00:41:35.480 --> 00:41:37.840
Well, we need you there to tailor compounds

579
00:41:37.840 --> 00:41:39.840
specific to our needs.

580
00:41:39.840 --> 00:41:40.680
Which are?

581
00:41:40.680 --> 00:41:42.000
Great depth.

582
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:44.080
A dream within a dream.

583
00:41:44.080 --> 00:41:47.900
Two levels.

584
00:41:47.900 --> 00:41:49.300
Three.

585
00:41:49.300 --> 00:41:50.620
Not possible.

586
00:41:50.620 --> 00:41:52.740
That many dreams within dreams is too unstable.

587
00:41:52.740 --> 00:41:55.380
It is possible.

588
00:41:55.380 --> 00:41:56.940
You just have to have a sedative.

589
00:41:57.780 --> 00:42:02.840
A powerful sedative.

590
00:42:02.840 --> 00:42:03.920
Five.

591
00:42:03.920 --> 00:42:06.450
Six.

592
00:42:06.450 --> 00:42:09.170
The only way to know you've done the job.

593
00:42:09.170 --> 00:42:10.690
Easy if I were you with you.

594
00:42:10.690 --> 00:42:14.050
There's no room for tourists on a job like this, Mr. Seddon.

595
00:42:14.050 --> 00:42:16.050
This time, it seems there is.

596
00:42:17.290 --> 00:42:19.850
This, I think, is a good place to start.

597
00:42:19.850 --> 00:42:21.330
I use it every day.

598
00:42:21.330 --> 00:42:22.570
My form?

599
00:42:22.570 --> 00:42:27.700
Yeah, I'll show you.

600
00:42:27.700 --> 00:42:45.120
Perhaps you will not want to see after you.

601
00:42:45.120 --> 00:42:46.320
Can I do it by the house?

602
00:42:46.320 --> 00:42:51.000
I come every day to share the dream.

603
00:42:51.000 --> 00:42:52.480
You see?

604
00:42:52.480 --> 00:42:59.440
Very stable.

605
00:42:59.440 --> 00:43:01.000
How long do they dream for?

606
00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:03.800
Three, four hours each day.

607
00:43:03.800 --> 00:43:05.040
In dream time?

608
00:43:05.040 --> 00:43:06.920
With this compound?

609
00:43:06.920 --> 00:43:08.760
About 40 hours each and every day.

610
00:43:08.760 --> 00:43:10.200
Why do they do it?

611
00:43:10.200 --> 00:43:13.700
Tell him, Mr. Cobb.

612
00:43:13.700 --> 00:43:16.460
After a while, it becomes the only way you can dream.

613
00:43:16.460 --> 00:43:18.900
You're used to the dream, Mr. Cobb.

614
00:43:18.900 --> 00:43:20.820
They come here every day to sleep.

615
00:43:20.820 --> 00:43:23.940
No.

616
00:43:23.940 --> 00:43:27.860
They come.

617
00:43:27.860 --> 00:43:36.550
The dream has become the reality.

618
00:43:36.550 --> 00:44:00.860
Let's see what you can do.

619
00:44:00.860 --> 00:44:18.470
Sharp, no?

620
00:44:18.470 --> 00:44:19.310
Mr. Cobb?

621
00:44:20.830 --> 00:44:22.670
Yeah, yeah.

622
00:44:22.670 --> 00:44:32.960
Everything's just fine.

623
00:44:32.960 --> 00:44:34.320
Robert Fisher.

624
00:44:34.320 --> 00:44:36.880
He is the Fisher-Maro Energic New Armor.

625
00:44:36.880 --> 00:44:38.720
What's your problem with this, Mr. Fisher?

626
00:44:38.720 --> 00:44:40.880
That's not your concern.

627
00:44:40.880 --> 00:44:45.480
Mr. Sido, this isn't your typical corporate espionage.

628
00:44:45.480 --> 00:44:47.040
You asked me for inception.

629
00:44:47.040 --> 00:44:50.280
I do hope you understand the gravity of that request.

630
00:44:51.520 --> 00:44:53.720
The seed that we plant in this man's mind

631
00:44:53.720 --> 00:44:54.720
will grow into an idea.

632
00:44:54.720 --> 00:44:56.960
This idea will define him.

633
00:44:56.960 --> 00:44:59.160
It may come to change.

634
00:44:59.160 --> 00:45:01.600
It may come to change everything about him.

635
00:45:01.600 --> 00:45:03.480
We are the last company standing between them

636
00:45:03.480 --> 00:45:05.840
on total energy dominance.

637
00:45:05.840 --> 00:45:08.200
We can no longer compete.

638
00:45:08.200 --> 00:45:10.200
Soon, they'll control the energy supply

639
00:45:10.200 --> 00:45:11.600
without the world.

640
00:45:11.600 --> 00:45:14.080
In effect, they become a new superpower.

641
00:45:15.520 --> 00:45:18.400
The wall needs Robert Fisher to change his mind.

642
00:45:19.280 --> 00:45:20.520
That's where we come in.

643
00:45:20.520 --> 00:45:23.840
How is Robert Fisher's relationship with his father?

644
00:45:23.840 --> 00:45:27.000
Rumor is the relationship is quite complicated.

645
00:45:27.000 --> 00:45:29.600
We can't work based solely on rumor, can we?

646
00:45:29.600 --> 00:45:33.280
Can you get me access to this man here, Browning?

647
00:45:33.280 --> 00:45:37.320
Fisher Sr.'s right-hand man, Fisher Jr.'s godfather.

648
00:45:37.320 --> 00:45:38.880
It should be possible,

649
00:45:38.880 --> 00:45:40.640
if you can get the right references.

650
00:45:40.640 --> 00:45:43.320
References are something of a speciality

651
00:45:43.320 --> 00:45:46.390
for being missed as I do.

652
00:45:46.390 --> 00:45:48.350
Not smelling settlement here.

653
00:45:48.350 --> 00:45:49.190
Take him down.

654
00:45:49.190 --> 00:45:51.230
Mr. Browning, Maurice Fisher's policy

655
00:45:51.230 --> 00:45:57.940
is always one of avoiding litigation.

656
00:45:58.020 --> 00:46:01.700
We voice your concerns with Maurice directly.

657
00:46:01.700 --> 00:46:02.740
I'm not sure that's necessary.

658
00:46:02.740 --> 00:46:29.480
No, no, no, I think we should.

659
00:46:29.480 --> 00:46:31.760
I don't want to bother him unnecessarily, but...

660
00:46:31.760 --> 00:46:34.200
Robert, it's up to you.

661
00:46:34.200 --> 00:46:36.880
Keep out of the damn way.

662
00:46:36.880 --> 00:46:37.720
So do it.

663
00:46:37.720 --> 00:46:39.440
Get to it.

664
00:46:39.440 --> 00:46:41.560
Put it through.

665
00:46:41.560 --> 00:46:45.200
Never, never, never to say, as I ask.

666
00:46:46.400 --> 00:46:56.360
Leave them.

667
00:46:56.360 --> 00:46:57.800
A cherished memory of his.

668
00:46:58.840 --> 00:47:00.200
I put it beside his bed.

669
00:47:01.360 --> 00:47:02.600
He hasn't even noticed.

670
00:47:03.760 --> 00:47:09.890
Robert, we need to talk about a power of attorney.

671
00:47:09.890 --> 00:47:10.730
I know this is our time.

672
00:47:10.730 --> 00:47:11.570
Not now, I'm prepared.

673
00:47:11.570 --> 00:47:17.460
But it's imperative that we start to...

674
00:47:17.460 --> 00:47:19.340
The vultures are circling.

675
00:47:19.340 --> 00:47:21.060
The sicker Maurice Fisher becomes,

676
00:47:21.060 --> 00:47:23.940
the more powerful Peter Browning becomes.

677
00:47:23.940 --> 00:47:27.020
I've had ample opportunity to observe Browning,

678
00:47:27.020 --> 00:47:28.460
adopt his physical presence,

679
00:47:28.460 --> 00:47:31.420
study his mannerisms, and so on and so forth.

680
00:47:31.420 --> 00:47:33.100
So now in the first layer of the dream,

681
00:47:33.100 --> 00:47:34.580
I can impersonate Browning

682
00:47:35.580 --> 00:47:38.580
and suggest concepts to Fisher's conscious mind.

683
00:47:38.580 --> 00:47:40.500
Then when we take him a level deeper,

684
00:47:40.500 --> 00:47:42.900
his own projection of Browning should,

685
00:47:42.900 --> 00:47:44.700
should feed that right back to him.

686
00:47:44.700 --> 00:47:46.700
So he gives himself the idea?

687
00:47:46.700 --> 00:47:47.540
Precisely.

688
00:47:48.380 --> 00:47:49.300
It's the only way it will stick.

689
00:47:49.300 --> 00:47:50.900
It has to see himself generated.

690
00:47:50.900 --> 00:47:53.420
Eames, I am impressed.

691
00:47:54.460 --> 00:47:56.220
Your condescension, as always,

692
00:47:56.220 --> 00:47:57.300
is much appreciated, Arthur.

693
00:47:57.300 --> 00:47:58.140
Thank you.

694
00:47:58.140 --> 00:48:21.470
Are you going under on your own?

695
00:48:21.470 --> 00:48:25.590
No, no, it's just running some experiments.

696
00:48:25.950 --> 00:48:27.750
I didn't realize anyone was here.

697
00:48:27.750 --> 00:48:28.590
Yeah, I was just,

698
00:48:28.590 --> 00:48:30.470
I was working on my totem, actually.

699
00:48:30.470 --> 00:48:31.750
Here, take a look.

700
00:48:34.060 --> 00:48:35.300
So you're learning, huh?

701
00:48:35.300 --> 00:48:38.020
An elegant solution for keeping track of reality.

702
00:48:39.660 --> 00:48:40.620
Was it your idea?

703
00:48:40.620 --> 00:48:43.180
No, it was, it was Moll's, actually.

704
00:48:43.180 --> 00:48:45.820
This, this one was hers.

705
00:48:45.820 --> 00:48:50.090
She'd spin it in the dream, it would never topple.

706
00:48:50.090 --> 00:48:53.330
Spin and spin.

707
00:48:53.330 --> 00:48:57.260
Arthur told me she passed away.

708
00:48:57.260 --> 00:48:59.220
How are the mazes coming along?

709
00:48:59.220 --> 00:49:00.860
Each level relates to the part

710
00:49:00.860 --> 00:49:03.700
of the subject's subconscious that we are trying to access.

711
00:49:03.700 --> 00:49:06.820
So, making the bottom level a hospital,

712
00:49:06.820 --> 00:49:08.640
so Fisher will bring his father.

713
00:49:10.860 --> 00:49:12.780
Actually, I have a question about this layout.

714
00:49:12.780 --> 00:49:15.220
No, no, no, don't, don't show me specifics.

715
00:49:15.220 --> 00:49:18.060
Only the dreamers should know the layout.

716
00:49:18.060 --> 00:49:19.260
Why is that so important?

717
00:49:19.260 --> 00:49:21.260
In case one of us brings in our projections,

718
00:49:21.260 --> 00:49:23.780
we don't want them knowing the details of the maze.

719
00:49:25.060 --> 00:49:27.580
You mean in case you bring Moll in?

720
00:49:27.580 --> 00:49:31.140
You can't keep her out, can you?

721
00:49:31.140 --> 00:49:31.980
Right.

722
00:49:31.980 --> 00:49:34.940
She can't build because if you know the maze,

723
00:49:34.940 --> 00:49:36.140
then she knows it.

724
00:49:36.140 --> 00:49:38.780
Well, she'd sabotage the whole operation.

725
00:49:38.780 --> 00:49:39.980
Cobb, do the others know?

726
00:49:39.980 --> 00:49:41.420
No, they don't.

727
00:49:41.420 --> 00:49:43.460
You've gotta warn them if this is getting worse.

728
00:49:43.460 --> 00:49:47.060
No one said it's getting worse.

729
00:49:47.060 --> 00:49:48.140
I need to get home.

730
00:49:48.140 --> 00:49:49.940
That's all I care about right now.

731
00:49:51.180 --> 00:49:56.460
Why can't you go home?

732
00:49:56.460 --> 00:50:01.730
Because they think I killed them.

733
00:50:01.730 --> 00:50:03.370
Thank you.

734
00:50:03.370 --> 00:50:04.330
For what?

735
00:50:04.330 --> 00:50:06.650
For not asking whether I did.

736
00:50:06.650 --> 00:50:08.930
I was split up with my father's empire.

737
00:50:08.930 --> 00:50:11.450
Now, this is obviously an idea that Robert himself

738
00:50:11.970 --> 00:50:13.530
would choose to reject,

739
00:50:13.530 --> 00:50:16.250
which is why we need to plant it deep in his subconscious.

740
00:50:16.250 --> 00:50:19.370
The subconscious is motivated by emotion, right?

741
00:50:19.370 --> 00:50:20.210
Not reason.

742
00:50:20.210 --> 00:50:22.090
We need to find a way to translate this

743
00:50:22.090 --> 00:50:23.690
into an emotional concept.

744
00:50:23.690 --> 00:50:26.530
How do you translate a business strategy into an emotion?

745
00:50:26.530 --> 00:50:27.970
That's what we're here to figure out, right?

746
00:50:27.970 --> 00:50:29.970
Now, Robert's relationship with his father

747
00:50:29.970 --> 00:50:31.890
is stress, to say the least.

748
00:50:31.890 --> 00:50:32.730
Well, can we run with that?

749
00:50:32.730 --> 00:50:35.450
Who could suggest to him breaking up his father's company

750
00:50:35.450 --> 00:50:36.850
as a screw you to the old man?

751
00:50:36.850 --> 00:50:38.930
No, because I think positive emotion

752
00:50:38.930 --> 00:50:40.650
trumps negative emotion every time.

753
00:50:40.650 --> 00:50:44.650
We all yearn for reconciliation or catharsis.

754
00:50:44.650 --> 00:50:45.770
We need Robert Fisher to have

755
00:50:45.770 --> 00:50:48.530
a positive emotional reaction to all this.

756
00:50:48.530 --> 00:50:49.530
I will try this.

757
00:50:50.690 --> 00:50:53.610
My father accepts that I want to create for myself

758
00:50:53.610 --> 00:50:55.850
not following his footsteps.

759
00:50:55.850 --> 00:50:56.890
That might work.

760
00:50:56.890 --> 00:50:57.730
Might.

761
00:50:58.650 --> 00:51:00.610
We're gonna need to do a little better than might.

762
00:51:00.610 --> 00:51:02.330
Thank you for your contribution, Arthur.

763
00:51:02.330 --> 00:51:05.450
Forgive me for wanting a little specificity, Eames.

764
00:51:05.450 --> 00:51:06.730
Specificity?

765
00:51:06.730 --> 00:51:08.730
Inception's not about being specific.

766
00:51:08.730 --> 00:51:10.090
When we get inside his mind,

767
00:51:10.570 --> 00:51:13.740
we're gonna have to work with what we find.

768
00:51:13.740 --> 00:51:14.980
On the top level,

769
00:51:14.980 --> 00:51:17.300
we open up his relationship with his father.

770
00:51:17.300 --> 00:51:20.460
Say, I will not follow in my father's footsteps.

771
00:51:20.460 --> 00:51:22.860
Then the next level down, we feed him.

772
00:51:22.860 --> 00:51:25.340
I will create something for myself.

773
00:51:25.340 --> 00:51:27.380
Then, by the time we hit the bottom level,

774
00:51:27.380 --> 00:51:28.660
we bring out the big guns.

775
00:51:28.660 --> 00:51:30.260
My father doesn't want me to be him.

776
00:51:30.260 --> 00:51:31.100
Exactly.

777
00:51:32.140 --> 00:51:34.900
Three layers down, dreams are gonna collapse

778
00:51:34.900 --> 00:51:36.540
with the slightest disturbance.

779
00:51:36.540 --> 00:51:39.100
Sedation, for sleep.

780
00:51:39.100 --> 00:51:41.100
Sable enough to create three layers of dreaming,

781
00:51:41.100 --> 00:51:41.940
we'll have to combine it

782
00:51:41.940 --> 00:51:56.520
with an extremely powerful sedative.

783
00:51:56.520 --> 00:51:57.360
Goodnight.

784
00:51:58.240 --> 00:51:59.960
The compound we'll be using to share the dream

785
00:51:59.960 --> 00:52:01.920
creates a very clear connection between dreamers

786
00:52:01.920 --> 00:52:04.800
whilst actually accelerating brain function.

787
00:52:04.800 --> 00:52:06.960
In other words, it gives us more time on each level.

788
00:52:06.960 --> 00:52:08.040
Brain function in the dream

789
00:52:08.040 --> 00:52:10.240
will be about 20 times normal.

790
00:52:10.240 --> 00:52:12.640
When you enter a dream within that dream,

791
00:52:12.640 --> 00:52:13.680
the effect is compounded.

792
00:52:13.680 --> 00:52:15.080
It's three dreams, that's 10 hours,

793
00:52:15.080 --> 00:52:15.920
times 20. I'm sorry.

794
00:52:15.920 --> 00:52:17.680
Mass was never my strong subject.

795
00:52:17.680 --> 00:52:19.200
How much time is that?

796
00:52:19.200 --> 00:52:21.200
It's a week, the first level down.

797
00:52:22.160 --> 00:52:23.840
Six months, the second level down,

798
00:52:23.840 --> 00:52:25.520
and the third level.

799
00:52:25.520 --> 00:52:29.810
It's 10 years.

800
00:52:29.810 --> 00:52:32.370
Who would wanna be stuck in a dream for 10 years?

801
00:52:32.370 --> 00:52:33.730
Depends on the dream.

802
00:52:33.730 --> 00:52:36.730
So once we've made the plans, how do we get out?

803
00:52:36.730 --> 00:52:38.370
I'm hoping you have something more elegant in mind

804
00:52:38.370 --> 00:52:39.650
than shooting me in the head.

805
00:52:39.650 --> 00:52:41.210
A kick.

806
00:52:41.210 --> 00:52:42.530
What's a kick?

807
00:52:42.530 --> 00:52:47.520
This, I argue, would be a kick.

808
00:52:47.520 --> 00:52:48.880
It's that feeling of falling you get

809
00:52:48.880 --> 00:52:51.720
that jolts you awake, it snaps you out of the dream.

810
00:52:51.720 --> 00:52:53.560
Are we gonna feel a kick with this kind of sedation?

811
00:52:53.560 --> 00:52:54.760
Oh, that's the clever part.

812
00:52:54.800 --> 00:52:56.080
I customize the sedative

813
00:52:56.080 --> 00:52:58.280
to leave inner ear function unimpaired.

814
00:52:58.280 --> 00:53:01.000
That way, however deep the sleep,

815
00:53:01.000 --> 00:53:04.840
the sleeper still feels falling, or tipping.

816
00:53:06.360 --> 00:53:08.280
Trick is to synchronize a kick

817
00:53:08.280 --> 00:53:11.240
that can penetrate all three levels.

818
00:53:11.240 --> 00:53:12.520
We could use the musical countdown

819
00:53:12.520 --> 00:53:22.750
to synchronize the different kicks.

820
00:53:22.750 --> 00:53:26.590
Hasn't got any surgery scheduled, no dental, nothing.

821
00:53:26.590 --> 00:53:28.350
Well, isn't he supposed to have a knee operation?

822
00:53:28.350 --> 00:53:29.230
Nothing.

823
00:53:29.230 --> 00:53:30.670
Nothing that I've put him under for anyway,

824
00:53:30.710 --> 00:53:33.670
we need, we need at least a good 10 hours.

825
00:53:33.670 --> 00:53:35.150
Sin Nito, Los Angeles.

826
00:53:36.470 --> 00:53:38.470
One of the longest flights in the world.

827
00:53:38.470 --> 00:53:40.870
He makes it every two weeks.

828
00:53:40.870 --> 00:53:43.710
Well, he must be flying private then.

829
00:53:43.710 --> 00:53:46.950
Not if there were unexpected maintenance with his plane.

830
00:53:46.950 --> 00:53:48.630
It'd have to be a 747.

831
00:53:48.630 --> 00:53:49.470
Why is that?

832
00:53:49.470 --> 00:53:51.190
It's on a 747, the pilot's up top,

833
00:53:51.190 --> 00:53:52.910
the first-class cabin's in the nose,

834
00:53:52.910 --> 00:53:54.350
so no one would walk through.

835
00:53:54.350 --> 00:53:56.070
But you'd have to buy out the entire cabin

836
00:53:56.070 --> 00:53:57.990
and the first-class flight attendant.

837
00:53:58.030 --> 00:54:04.900
I bought the yellow, Sin Nito.

838
00:54:04.900 --> 00:54:08.260
Looks like we have our 10 hours.

839
00:54:08.260 --> 00:55:46.700
Ariadne, terrific work, by the way.

840
00:55:46.700 --> 00:55:48.100
I share dreams with you.

841
00:55:48.100 --> 00:56:03.400
Not these, these are my dreams.

842
00:56:03.400 --> 00:56:04.680
You do this to yourself?

843
00:56:05.960 --> 00:56:10.490
It's the only way I can still dream.

844
00:56:10.490 --> 00:56:12.250
Why is it so important to dream?

845
00:56:13.610 --> 00:56:33.720
My dreams were still together.

846
00:56:33.720 --> 00:56:34.840
These are memories,

847
00:56:34.840 --> 00:56:36.920
and you said never to use memories.

848
00:56:36.920 --> 00:56:41.090
I know I did.

849
00:56:41.090 --> 00:56:43.610
You can't let her go.

850
00:56:43.650 --> 00:56:44.930
I understand.

851
00:56:44.930 --> 00:56:46.290
These are moments I regret.

852
00:56:46.290 --> 00:56:50.350
They're memories that I have to change.

853
00:56:50.350 --> 00:56:52.750
Well, what's done there that you regret?

854
00:56:52.750 --> 00:56:54.030
Listen, there's only one thing

855
00:56:54.030 --> 00:57:04.730
you need to understand about me.

856
00:57:04.730 --> 00:57:05.770
This is your house?

857
00:57:06.930 --> 00:57:08.330
Mine and Moll's, yes.

858
00:57:09.730 --> 00:57:10.570
Where is she?

859
00:57:11.890 --> 00:57:18.980
She's already gone.

860
00:57:18.980 --> 00:57:21.660
My son, James, he's digging for something.

861
00:57:21.660 --> 00:57:24.860
Maybe a worm.

862
00:57:24.860 --> 00:57:26.460
That's Philippa.

863
00:57:26.460 --> 00:57:28.260
See, I thought about calling out to them

864
00:57:28.260 --> 00:57:32.340
so they'd turn and smile and I could see those.

865
00:57:32.340 --> 00:57:37.270
Beautiful faces of theirs, but it's all too late.

866
00:57:37.270 --> 00:57:47.160
Right now, or never come.

867
00:57:47.160 --> 00:57:48.600
I'm gonna regret this moment,

868
00:57:48.600 --> 00:57:55.430
and I need to see their faces one last time.

869
00:57:55.430 --> 00:57:59.740
The moment's past.

870
00:57:59.740 --> 00:58:04.040
Whatever I do, I can't change this moment.

871
00:58:04.040 --> 00:58:07.190
I'm about to call out to them.

872
00:58:07.190 --> 00:58:10.920
They run away.

873
00:58:10.920 --> 00:58:12.640
If I'm ever gonna see their faces again,

874
00:58:12.640 --> 00:58:58.400
I've gotta get back home, in the real world.

875
00:58:58.400 --> 00:58:59.800
What are you doing here?

876
00:59:00.920 --> 00:59:03.240
James, I know who you are.

877
00:59:03.240 --> 00:59:14.050
What are you doing here?

878
00:59:14.050 --> 00:59:15.930
I'm trying to understand.

879
00:59:15.930 --> 00:59:19.260
How could you understand?

880
00:59:19.260 --> 00:59:23.350
Do you know what it is to be a lover?

881
00:59:23.350 --> 00:59:26.890
To be half in a hole?

882
00:59:26.890 --> 00:59:30.160
No.

883
00:59:30.160 --> 00:59:33.230
Until you're real.

884
00:59:33.230 --> 00:59:36.660
You're waiting for a train.

885
00:59:36.660 --> 00:59:41.120
A train that will take you far away.

886
00:59:41.120 --> 00:59:43.680
You know where you hope this train will take you.

887
00:59:45.200 --> 00:59:46.760
But you don't know for sure.

888
00:59:47.800 --> 00:59:49.040
But it doesn't matter.

889
00:59:50.440 --> 00:59:52.120
How can it not matter to you

890
00:59:52.120 --> 00:59:53.960
what a train will take you?

891
00:59:53.960 --> 00:59:56.940
Because we'll be together.

892
00:59:56.940 --> 00:59:58.660
How could you bring her here, Dom?

893
00:59:58.660 --> 01:00:00.970
What is this place?

894
01:00:00.970 --> 01:00:03.710
Tell us who you are, you sister.

895
01:00:03.710 --> 01:00:17.580
What happened here?

896
01:00:17.580 --> 01:00:36.600
I promise.

897
01:00:36.600 --> 01:00:38.880
Do you think you can just build

898
01:00:38.880 --> 01:00:41.000
a prison of memories to lock her in?

899
01:00:42.720 --> 01:00:45.840
Do you really think that that's gonna contain her?

900
01:00:45.840 --> 01:00:46.680
It's time.

901
01:00:48.160 --> 01:00:50.840
Morris Fisher just died in Sydney.

902
01:00:50.840 --> 01:00:51.800
When's the funeral?

903
01:00:51.800 --> 01:00:53.360
Thursday, in Los Angeles.

904
01:00:53.360 --> 01:00:54.600
Robert should accompany the body

905
01:00:54.600 --> 01:00:55.720
no later than Tuesday.

906
01:00:55.720 --> 01:00:58.740
We should move him.

907
01:00:58.740 --> 01:01:01.820
Carbo, I'm coming with you.

908
01:01:01.820 --> 01:01:03.180
The team needs someone

909
01:01:03.180 --> 01:01:07.510
who understands what you're struggling with.

910
01:01:07.510 --> 01:01:09.790
And it doesn't have to be me.

911
01:01:09.790 --> 01:01:19.060
But then you have to show Arthur what I just saw.

912
01:01:19.060 --> 01:01:24.800
Get us another seat on the plane.

913
01:01:24.800 --> 01:01:26.000
If I get on this plane

914
01:01:26.000 --> 01:01:28.320
and you don't honor our agreement,

915
01:01:28.320 --> 01:01:31.080
when we land, I go to jail for the rest of my life.

916
01:01:32.280 --> 01:01:34.680
Don't take that job en route.

917
01:01:34.680 --> 01:01:37.280
I make one phone call from the plane.

918
01:01:37.280 --> 01:02:34.120
You have no trouble getting through immigration.

919
01:02:34.120 --> 01:02:35.680
Sir, drop it.

920
01:02:35.680 --> 01:02:37.280
Can you gentlemen care for the drink?

921
01:02:37.280 --> 01:02:38.120
Water, please.

922
01:02:39.040 --> 01:02:39.880
Same.

923
01:02:44.160 --> 01:02:45.400
Thank you.

924
01:02:45.400 --> 01:02:46.640
You know, I couldn't help but notice,

925
01:02:46.640 --> 01:02:48.200
but you wouldn't happen to be related

926
01:02:48.200 --> 01:02:51.120
to the Morris Fisher, would you?

927
01:02:51.120 --> 01:02:54.680
Yes, he was my father.

928
01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:57.880
Well, he was a very inspiring figure.

929
01:02:57.880 --> 01:02:59.240
I'm sorry for your loss.

930
01:03:02.980 --> 01:03:03.820
Here you go.

931
01:03:03.820 --> 01:03:04.780
Thank you.

932
01:03:04.780 --> 01:03:07.260
Hey, to your father.

933
01:03:08.780 --> 01:04:21.550
May he rest in peace, huh?

934
01:04:21.550 --> 01:04:23.430
Bit too much free champagne with one take-off,

935
01:04:23.430 --> 01:04:24.270
may he, sir?

936
01:04:25.150 --> 01:04:40.340
I know he's gonna be looking for a taxi in this one.

937
01:04:40.340 --> 01:04:41.660
Asshole!

938
01:04:41.660 --> 01:04:42.580
Hey, man, why don't you try?

939
01:04:42.580 --> 01:04:43.420
Walk away.

940
01:05:01.420 --> 01:05:02.900
All right, taxi!

941
01:05:02.900 --> 01:05:06.610
Thank you.

942
01:05:06.610 --> 01:05:08.370
All right, third market.

943
01:05:08.370 --> 01:05:09.210
Oh, snap.

944
01:05:10.330 --> 01:05:11.410
What are you doing?

945
01:05:11.410 --> 01:05:12.450
I'm sorry, I thought it was free.

946
01:05:12.450 --> 01:05:13.290
Well, it's not.

947
01:05:13.290 --> 01:05:14.130
Maybe we could share.

948
01:05:14.130 --> 01:05:14.970
Maybe not.

949
01:05:14.970 --> 01:05:26.360
Can you pull over and get this?

950
01:05:26.360 --> 01:05:39.010
Come on!

951
01:05:39.010 --> 01:05:40.330
$500 in there.

952
01:05:40.330 --> 01:05:41.610
My wallet's worth more than that.

953
01:05:41.610 --> 01:05:43.690
So you might at least drop me at my stop.

954
01:05:43.690 --> 01:06:02.110
I'm afraid it doesn't work.

955
01:06:02.150 --> 01:07:10.590
It wasn't in the design.

956
01:07:10.590 --> 01:07:12.550
This is okay, unless it gets caustic.

957
01:07:12.550 --> 01:07:44.140
Sato, buy a freight train.

958
01:07:44.140 --> 01:07:45.180
Why would you put a train crossing

959
01:07:45.180 --> 01:07:46.420
in the middle of a downtown intersection?

960
01:07:46.420 --> 01:07:47.260
I didn't.

961
01:07:47.260 --> 01:07:48.100
Well, where'd it come from?

962
01:07:48.100 --> 01:07:48.940
Well, let me ask you a question.

963
01:07:48.940 --> 01:07:50.340
Why the hell were we ambushed, huh?

964
01:07:50.340 --> 01:07:51.780
Those were not normal projections.

965
01:07:51.780 --> 01:07:53.060
They've been trained for God's sakes.

966
01:07:53.060 --> 01:07:53.900
You're right.

967
01:07:53.900 --> 01:07:54.740
How could he be trained?

968
01:07:54.740 --> 01:07:57.660
Fishers had an extractor teach his subconscious

969
01:07:57.660 --> 01:08:00.820
to defend itself, so his subconscious is militarized.

970
01:08:00.820 --> 01:08:01.900
It should have shown in the research.

971
01:08:01.900 --> 01:08:02.740
I'm sorry.

972
01:08:02.740 --> 01:08:04.180
So why the hell didn't it?

973
01:08:04.180 --> 01:08:05.860
Don't tell me to calm down.

974
01:08:05.860 --> 01:08:07.460
This was your job, God damn it.

975
01:08:07.500 --> 01:08:08.980
This was your responsibility.

976
01:08:08.980 --> 01:08:11.260
You were meant to check Fisher's background thoroughly.

977
01:08:11.260 --> 01:08:13.020
We are not prepared for this type of violence.

978
01:08:13.020 --> 01:08:15.020
We have dealt with sub-security before.

979
01:08:15.020 --> 01:08:16.100
We'll be a little more careful,

980
01:08:16.100 --> 01:08:16.940
and we're gonna be fine.

981
01:08:16.940 --> 01:08:18.140
This was not a part of the plan.

982
01:08:18.140 --> 01:08:19.380
He's dying, for God's sake.

983
01:08:19.380 --> 01:08:20.620
All right, let's put him out of his misery.

984
01:08:20.620 --> 01:08:21.820
Don't do that.

985
01:08:21.820 --> 01:08:23.220
Don't do that.

986
01:08:23.220 --> 01:08:24.100
He's in agony.

987
01:08:24.100 --> 01:08:25.420
I'm waking him up.

988
01:08:25.420 --> 01:08:27.540
No, it won't wake him up.

989
01:08:27.540 --> 01:08:29.380
What do you mean, it won't wake him up?

990
01:08:29.380 --> 01:08:31.180
When we die in a dream, we wake up.

991
01:08:31.180 --> 01:08:32.780
Not from this.

992
01:08:32.780 --> 01:08:34.980
Would you have it sedated to wake up that way?

993
01:08:35.860 --> 01:08:37.700
Right, so what happens when we die?

994
01:08:37.700 --> 01:08:38.620
I drop in a limbo.

995
01:08:38.620 --> 01:08:39.580
Are you serious?

996
01:08:39.580 --> 01:08:40.540
Limbo?

997
01:08:40.540 --> 01:08:42.380
Unconstructed dream space.

998
01:08:42.380 --> 01:08:43.660
Well, what the hell is down there?

999
01:08:43.660 --> 01:08:45.860
Just raw, infinite subconscious.

1000
01:08:45.860 --> 01:08:47.300
Nothing is down there,

1001
01:08:47.300 --> 01:08:48.940
except for whatever might have been left behind

1002
01:08:48.940 --> 01:08:50.140
by anyone sharing the dream

1003
01:08:50.140 --> 01:08:51.980
who's been trapped there before,

1004
01:08:51.980 --> 01:08:54.300
which in our case, is just you.

1005
01:08:54.300 --> 01:08:55.980
Well, how long can we be stuck there?

1006
01:08:55.980 --> 01:08:57.860
Can't even think about trying to escape in two.

1007
01:08:57.860 --> 01:08:59.500
This sedation is eased. How long?

1008
01:08:59.500 --> 01:09:01.260
Decades, it could be infinite, I don't know.

1009
01:09:01.260 --> 01:09:02.940
Ask him, he's the one who's been there.

1010
01:09:02.940 --> 01:09:04.380
Just get him upstairs.

1011
01:09:06.160 --> 01:09:07.000
Great.

1012
01:09:08.440 --> 01:09:09.280
Thank you.

1013
01:09:10.600 --> 01:09:12.520
So, now we're trapped in Fisher's mind

1014
01:09:12.520 --> 01:09:13.880
battling his own private army,

1015
01:09:13.880 --> 01:09:16.720
and if we get killed, we'll be lost in limbo

1016
01:09:16.720 --> 01:09:18.440
till our brains turn to scrambled egg.

1017
01:09:18.440 --> 01:09:27.340
What have you got for us, Dave?

1018
01:09:30.220 --> 01:09:32.580
So you knew about these risks, and you didn't tell us?

1019
01:09:32.580 --> 01:09:33.700
There weren't meant to be any risks.

1020
01:09:33.700 --> 01:09:35.820
I didn't know we'd be dealing with a load of gunfire.

1021
01:09:35.820 --> 01:09:36.660
You had no rights.

1022
01:09:36.660 --> 01:09:39.220
This was the only way to go three layers deep.

1023
01:09:39.220 --> 01:09:41.460
And you, you knew about this and went along with it.

1024
01:09:41.460 --> 01:09:42.300
I trusted him.

1025
01:09:42.340 --> 01:09:44.460
You trusted and went when he promised you half his share?

1026
01:09:44.460 --> 01:09:46.740
No, his whole share.

1027
01:09:46.740 --> 01:09:48.020
Besides, he said he'd done it before.

1028
01:09:48.020 --> 01:09:48.860
We've done it before.

1029
01:09:48.860 --> 01:09:49.820
What, with Mal?

1030
01:09:49.820 --> 01:09:50.820
Cause that worked so good.

1031
01:09:50.820 --> 01:09:51.660
It has nothing to do with it.

1032
01:09:51.660 --> 01:09:53.740
I did what I had to do to get back to my children.

1033
01:09:53.740 --> 01:09:55.900
So you led us into a war zone with no way out.

1034
01:09:55.900 --> 01:09:56.900
There is a way out, all right.

1035
01:09:56.900 --> 01:09:58.620
We continue on with the job,

1036
01:09:58.620 --> 01:10:00.140
and we do it as fast as possible,

1037
01:10:00.140 --> 01:10:02.820
and we get out using the kick, just like before.

1038
01:10:02.820 --> 01:10:05.180
Forget it, we go any deeper, we just raise the stakes.

1039
01:10:05.180 --> 01:10:07.300
I am sitting this one out on this level, boys.

1040
01:10:07.300 --> 01:10:09.900
Fisher's security is surrounding this place as we speak.

1041
01:10:09.900 --> 01:10:12.340
10 hours of flight time is a week at this level.

1042
01:10:12.340 --> 01:10:14.780
That means each and every one of us will be killed.

1043
01:10:14.780 --> 01:10:16.700
That, I can guarantee you.

1044
01:10:16.700 --> 01:10:18.340
We have no other choice but to continue on

1045
01:10:18.340 --> 01:10:22.080
and do it as fast as possible.

1046
01:10:22.080 --> 01:10:24.720
Downwards is the only way forwards.

1047
01:10:26.080 --> 01:10:27.520
Get ready.

1048
01:10:27.520 --> 01:10:34.580
You, come on, let's go shake him up.

1049
01:10:34.580 --> 01:10:37.820
I'm insured against kidnapping for up to 10 million.

1050
01:10:37.820 --> 01:10:38.740
It should be very simple.

1051
01:10:38.740 --> 01:10:39.940
Shut up!

1052
01:10:39.940 --> 01:10:40.780
It won't be.

1053
01:10:40.780 --> 01:10:42.780
In your father's office, below the bookshelves

1054
01:10:42.780 --> 01:10:44.380
is his personal safe.

1055
01:10:44.380 --> 01:10:45.780
We need the combination.

1056
01:10:46.460 --> 01:10:48.140
I don't know any safe.

1057
01:10:48.140 --> 01:10:52.700
That doesn't mean you don't know the combination.

1058
01:10:52.700 --> 01:11:01.630
Tell us what it is.

1059
01:11:01.630 --> 01:11:04.070
We have it on good authority, you do know.

1060
01:11:04.070 --> 01:11:06.150
Yeah, who's authority?

1061
01:11:07.670 --> 01:11:09.750
$500 this cost.

1062
01:11:09.750 --> 01:11:11.470
What's inside it?

1063
01:11:11.470 --> 01:11:20.350
Cash, cards, ID, and this.

1064
01:11:20.350 --> 01:11:21.190
Useful?

1065
01:11:22.670 --> 01:11:24.110
Maybe.

1066
01:11:24.110 --> 01:11:26.310
You're on, you've got an hour.

1067
01:11:26.310 --> 01:11:27.150
An hour?

1068
01:11:28.150 --> 01:11:30.470
I was supposed to have all night to correct this.

1069
01:11:30.470 --> 01:11:33.470
The insider wasn't supposed to be shot in the chest.

1070
01:11:33.470 --> 01:11:36.110
You've got one hour, now get us something useful, please.

1071
01:11:36.110 --> 01:11:53.240
The combination, I don't know it.

1072
01:11:53.240 --> 01:11:54.960
Why does Browning say you do?

1073
01:11:54.960 --> 01:11:56.160
I don't know.

1074
01:11:56.160 --> 01:11:58.680
Just let me, let me talk to him and I'll find out.

1075
01:11:58.680 --> 01:12:02.570
You have one hour.

1076
01:12:02.570 --> 01:12:03.410
Start talking.

1077
01:12:08.650 --> 01:12:09.490
You okay?

1078
01:12:09.490 --> 01:12:16.410
He was bad at me for two days.

1079
01:12:18.050 --> 01:12:20.290
They have someone with access to your father's office

1080
01:12:20.610 --> 01:12:22.290
and they're trying to open his safe.

1081
01:12:22.290 --> 01:12:23.130
Yeah.

1082
01:12:23.130 --> 01:12:25.810
They thought I'd know the combination, but I don't know it.

1083
01:12:25.810 --> 01:12:28.050
Yeah, only either do I, so.

1084
01:12:28.050 --> 01:12:29.450
What?

1085
01:12:29.450 --> 01:12:31.610
Maurice told me that when he passed,

1086
01:12:31.610 --> 01:12:33.010
you were the only one to be able to open it.

1087
01:12:33.010 --> 01:12:36.090
No, he never gave me any combination.

1088
01:12:36.090 --> 01:12:37.770
Maybe he did.

1089
01:12:37.770 --> 01:12:40.570
Maybe you just didn't know it was a combination.

1090
01:12:40.570 --> 01:12:41.530
Well, what then?

1091
01:12:41.530 --> 01:12:44.250
I don't know some meaningful combination of numbers

1092
01:12:44.250 --> 01:12:50.040
based on your experiences with Maurice.

1093
01:12:50.080 --> 01:12:54.000
We didn't have very many meaningful experiences together.

1094
01:12:54.880 --> 01:12:58.970
Perhaps after your mother died.

1095
01:12:58.970 --> 01:13:04.760
After my mother died, you know what he told me?

1096
01:13:04.760 --> 01:13:08.200
There's really nothing to be said.

1097
01:13:08.200 --> 01:13:10.840
Oh, well, he was bad with emotion.

1098
01:13:10.840 --> 01:13:13.360
I was 11, Uncle Peter.

1099
01:13:14.600 --> 01:13:15.440
How's he doing?

1100
01:13:16.600 --> 01:13:18.040
He's in a lot of pain.

1101
01:13:18.040 --> 01:13:19.360
Get down to the lower levels,

1102
01:13:19.360 --> 01:13:20.960
the pain will be less intense.

1103
01:13:21.840 --> 01:13:22.840
And if he dies?

1104
01:13:23.840 --> 01:13:26.320
Worst case scenario, when he wakes up,

1105
01:13:26.320 --> 01:13:28.240
his mind is completely gone.

1106
01:13:28.240 --> 01:13:35.620
I appreciate that, Saito, but when you wake up,

1107
01:13:35.620 --> 01:13:38.700
you won't even remember that we had an arrangement.

1108
01:13:38.700 --> 01:13:40.820
Limbo's gonna become your reality.

1109
01:13:40.820 --> 01:13:42.620
You're gonna be lost down there so long

1110
01:13:42.620 --> 01:13:47.960
that you're gonna become an old man

1111
01:13:47.960 --> 01:14:02.540
waiting to die alone.

1112
01:14:02.540 --> 01:14:05.180
Breeze, these people are gonna kill us

1113
01:14:05.180 --> 01:14:06.540
if we don't give them the combination.

1114
01:14:06.540 --> 01:14:07.500
They just went around someplace.

1115
01:14:07.500 --> 01:14:08.860
I heard them.

1116
01:14:08.860 --> 01:14:10.820
They're gonna lock us in that van

1117
01:14:10.980 --> 01:14:13.220
and then drive it into the river.

1118
01:14:13.220 --> 01:14:14.820
All right, what is he gonna say?

1119
01:14:15.700 --> 01:14:17.460
Something for you.

1120
01:14:17.460 --> 01:14:21.220
Maurice always said it was his most precious gift to you.

1121
01:14:22.340 --> 01:14:23.740
A will.

1122
01:14:23.740 --> 01:14:25.700
Maurice's will is with Port and Dunn.

1123
01:14:25.700 --> 01:14:26.860
That's an alternate.

1124
01:14:26.860 --> 01:14:29.380
This would supersede the other if you wanted to.

1125
01:14:29.380 --> 01:14:32.260
It splits up the component businesses of Fisher Morrow

1126
01:14:32.260 --> 01:14:35.300
and be the end of the entire empire as we know it.

1127
01:14:36.220 --> 01:14:38.140
Destroy my old inheritance.

1128
01:14:38.140 --> 01:14:42.380
I already suggest such a thing.

1129
01:14:42.420 --> 01:14:46.420
I just don't know.

1130
01:14:46.420 --> 01:14:47.500
He loved you, Robert.

1131
01:14:49.140 --> 01:14:50.740
In his own way.

1132
01:14:50.740 --> 01:14:53.880
In his own way.

1133
01:14:53.880 --> 01:14:58.270
At the end, he called me into his deathbed.

1134
01:14:59.310 --> 01:15:02.550
He could barely speak.

1135
01:15:02.550 --> 01:15:08.950
Took the trouble to tell me one last thing.

1136
01:15:08.950 --> 01:15:10.350
He pulled me close.

1137
01:15:10.350 --> 01:15:21.430
When he may come, one word.

1138
01:15:21.430 --> 01:15:29.140
Disappoint.

1139
01:15:29.140 --> 01:15:30.340
When were you in Limbo?

1140
01:15:31.940 --> 01:15:33.460
You might have the rest of the team

1141
01:15:33.460 --> 01:15:35.260
convinced to carry on with this job,

1142
01:15:35.260 --> 01:15:36.580
but they don't know the truth.

1143
01:15:37.220 --> 01:15:38.060
What truth?

1144
01:15:38.060 --> 01:15:39.860
The truth that at any minute,

1145
01:15:39.860 --> 01:15:42.460
you might bring a freight train through the wall.

1146
01:15:42.460 --> 01:15:46.500
The truth that Maul is bursting through your subconscious.

1147
01:15:46.500 --> 01:15:49.300
And the truth that as we go deeper into Fisher,

1148
01:15:49.300 --> 01:15:51.820
we're also going deeper into you.

1149
01:15:51.820 --> 01:15:59.140
And I'm not sure we're gonna like what we find.

1150
01:15:59.140 --> 01:16:00.700
We were working together.

1151
01:16:00.700 --> 01:16:04.500
We were exploring the concept of a dream within a dream.

1152
01:16:04.500 --> 01:16:05.700
I kept pushing things.

1153
01:16:05.700 --> 01:16:07.100
I wanted to go deeper and deeper.

1154
01:16:07.100 --> 01:16:09.180
I wanted to go further.

1155
01:16:10.180 --> 01:16:11.820
I just didn't understand the concept

1156
01:16:11.820 --> 01:16:15.140
that ours could turn into years down there.

1157
01:16:15.140 --> 01:16:16.460
That we could get trapped so deep

1158
01:16:16.460 --> 01:16:19.940
that when we wound up on the shore

1159
01:16:19.940 --> 01:16:31.220
of our own subconscious, we lost sight of what was real.

1160
01:16:31.300 --> 01:16:35.520
We created, we built the world for ourselves.

1161
01:16:35.520 --> 01:16:36.800
We did that for years.

1162
01:16:38.520 --> 01:16:41.970
We built our own world.

1163
01:16:41.970 --> 01:16:43.530
How long were you stuck there?

1164
01:16:44.810 --> 01:16:55.380
Something like 50 years.

1165
01:16:55.420 --> 01:16:58.260
Wasn't so bad at first feeling like gods.

1166
01:16:58.260 --> 01:17:01.500
The problem was knowing that none of it was real.

1167
01:17:01.500 --> 01:17:04.300
Eventually, it just became impossible

1168
01:17:04.300 --> 01:17:06.180
for me to live like that.

1169
01:17:06.180 --> 01:17:10.880
And what about for her?

1170
01:17:10.880 --> 01:17:12.280
She had locked something away,

1171
01:17:12.280 --> 01:17:16.220
something deep inside her.

1172
01:17:16.220 --> 01:17:17.820
The truth that she had once known

1173
01:17:17.820 --> 01:17:24.270
but then chose to forget.

1174
01:17:24.270 --> 01:17:28.300
Nimbo became her reality.

1175
01:17:28.300 --> 01:17:30.660
What happened when you woke up?

1176
01:17:30.660 --> 01:17:34.340
To wake up from that after years, after decades.

1177
01:17:35.340 --> 01:17:38.980
To become old souls thrown back into youth like that.

1178
01:17:40.660 --> 01:17:42.660
I knew something was wrong with her.

1179
01:17:42.660 --> 01:17:45.860
She just wouldn't admit it.

1180
01:17:45.860 --> 01:17:49.470
Eventually, she told me the truth.

1181
01:17:49.470 --> 01:17:52.030
Possessed by an idea.

1182
01:17:52.030 --> 01:17:57.030
This one very simple idea that changed everything.

1183
01:17:58.820 --> 01:18:00.700
That our world wasn't real.

1184
01:18:02.300 --> 01:18:05.420
That she needed to wake up to come back to reality.

1185
01:18:05.420 --> 01:18:19.100
That to get back home, we had to kill ourselves.

1186
01:18:19.100 --> 01:18:20.340
What about your children?

1187
01:18:21.420 --> 01:18:23.260
She thought they were projections

1188
01:18:23.260 --> 01:18:24.500
that our real children were waiting

1189
01:18:24.500 --> 01:18:25.620
for us up there somewhere.

1190
01:18:25.620 --> 01:18:26.860
I'm their mother!

1191
01:18:26.860 --> 01:18:27.700
Calm down!

1192
01:18:27.700 --> 01:18:29.420
Don't you think I can tell the difference?

1193
01:18:29.420 --> 01:18:31.460
If this is my dream, why can't I control this?

1194
01:18:31.460 --> 01:18:33.580
Because you don't know you're dreaming!

1195
01:18:33.580 --> 01:18:35.900
She was certain there was nothing I could do,

1196
01:18:35.900 --> 01:18:37.220
no matter how much I begged,

1197
01:18:37.220 --> 01:18:39.420
no matter how much I pleaded.

1198
01:18:39.420 --> 01:18:45.710
She wanted to do it, but she could not do it alone.

1199
01:18:45.710 --> 01:18:47.310
She loved me too much, so.

1200
01:18:48.750 --> 01:19:18.590
She came up with a plan on our anniversary.

1201
01:19:18.590 --> 01:19:20.390
Sweetheart, what are you doing?

1202
01:19:20.390 --> 01:19:21.430
Join me.

1203
01:19:21.430 --> 01:19:24.270
Just step back inside, all right?

1204
01:19:24.270 --> 01:19:25.910
Just step back inside now, come on.

1205
01:19:25.910 --> 01:19:26.750
No.

1206
01:19:27.870 --> 01:19:30.590
I'm going to jump and you're coming with me.

1207
01:19:30.590 --> 01:19:31.430
No, I'm not.

1208
01:19:32.750 --> 01:19:33.910
Now you listen to me.

1209
01:19:35.150 --> 01:19:38.790
If you jump, you're not gonna wake up, remember?

1210
01:19:38.790 --> 01:19:39.630
You're gonna die.

1211
01:19:39.630 --> 01:19:42.430
Now just step back inside, come on.

1212
01:19:42.430 --> 01:19:44.510
Step back inside so we can talk about this.

1213
01:19:44.550 --> 01:19:48.670
We've talked enough.

1214
01:19:48.670 --> 01:19:49.510
Mom.

1215
01:19:49.510 --> 01:19:57.510
Come out onto the ledge or I'll jump right now.

1216
01:19:57.510 --> 01:20:01.710
I'm gonna talk about this, all right?

1217
01:20:01.710 --> 01:20:08.940
I'm asking you to take a leap of faith.

1218
01:20:08.940 --> 01:20:10.740
You know I can't do that.

1219
01:20:10.740 --> 01:20:13.580
Take a second to think about her children.

1220
01:20:13.580 --> 01:20:14.620
Think about James.

1221
01:20:16.220 --> 01:20:17.860
Think about Phillip by now.

1222
01:20:17.860 --> 01:20:21.260
If I go without you, they'll take them away anyway.

1223
01:20:21.260 --> 01:20:22.460
What does that mean?

1224
01:20:22.460 --> 01:20:24.700
I filed a letter with our attorney

1225
01:20:24.700 --> 01:20:30.380
explaining how I'm fearful for my safety,

1226
01:20:30.380 --> 01:20:36.300
how you've threatened to kill me.

1227
01:20:36.300 --> 01:20:38.220
I love you, Donna.

1228
01:20:38.220 --> 01:20:39.060
Why did you?

1229
01:20:39.060 --> 01:20:39.900
Why would you do this to me?

1230
01:20:39.900 --> 01:20:43.100
I freed you from the Guild of Choosing to leave them.

1231
01:20:43.100 --> 01:20:46.100
We're going home to our real children.

1232
01:20:46.100 --> 01:20:46.940
No, no, no, no.

1233
01:20:46.940 --> 01:20:48.780
Mal, you listen to me, all right?

1234
01:20:48.780 --> 01:20:50.020
Mal, look at me, please.

1235
01:20:50.020 --> 01:20:51.780
You're waiting for a train.

1236
01:20:51.780 --> 01:20:53.820
Mal, goddammit, don't do this.

1237
01:20:53.820 --> 01:20:55.580
Train that will take you far away.

1238
01:20:55.580 --> 01:20:57.660
James and Philippa are waiting for you.

1239
01:20:57.660 --> 01:20:59.740
You know where you hope this train will take you.

1240
01:20:59.740 --> 01:21:00.580
They're waiting for us.

1241
01:21:00.580 --> 01:21:01.580
They come not so sure.

1242
01:21:01.580 --> 01:21:03.020
Mal, look at me.

1243
01:21:03.020 --> 01:21:04.220
That it doesn't matter.

1244
01:21:05.060 --> 01:21:05.900
Oh, goddammit.

1245
01:21:05.900 --> 01:21:07.460
Because you'll be together.

1246
01:21:07.460 --> 01:21:09.660
Sweetheart, look at me.

1247
01:21:09.660 --> 01:21:16.320
Oh, no, Jesus Christ.

1248
01:21:16.320 --> 01:21:18.520
She had herself declared sane

1249
01:21:18.520 --> 01:21:20.320
by three different psychiatrists.

1250
01:21:20.320 --> 01:21:22.920
It made it impossible for me to try to explain

1251
01:21:22.920 --> 01:21:24.720
the nature of her madness.

1252
01:21:24.720 --> 01:21:25.960
So I ran.

1253
01:21:27.680 --> 01:21:42.890
Right now or never come.

1254
01:21:42.890 --> 01:21:44.090
I left my children behind

1255
01:21:44.090 --> 01:21:47.250
and I've been trying to buy my way back ever since.

1256
01:21:47.250 --> 01:21:49.410
Your guilt defines her.

1257
01:21:49.410 --> 01:21:51.370
It's what powers her.

1258
01:21:51.370 --> 01:21:54.650
You are not responsible for the idea that destroyed her.

1259
01:21:55.730 --> 01:21:58.610
And if we are gonna succeed in this,

1260
01:21:58.610 --> 01:22:00.210
you have to forgive yourself

1261
01:22:01.450 --> 01:22:04.090
and you're gonna have to confront her.

1262
01:22:04.090 --> 01:22:05.810
But you don't have to do that alone.

1263
01:22:05.810 --> 01:22:06.650
No, no, no.

1264
01:22:06.650 --> 01:22:08.530
I'm doing it for the others.

1265
01:22:08.530 --> 01:22:10.490
Because they have no idea

1266
01:22:10.490 --> 01:22:20.590
the risk they've taken coming down here with you.

1267
01:22:20.590 --> 01:22:21.870
Time's up.

1268
01:22:21.870 --> 01:22:22.950
All right.

1269
01:22:22.950 --> 01:22:24.990
I don't know any combination.

1270
01:22:24.990 --> 01:22:26.190
Not consciously, anyway.

1271
01:22:26.230 --> 01:22:28.030
How about instinctively, huh?

1272
01:22:28.030 --> 01:22:29.950
I got somebody standing in your father's office

1273
01:22:29.950 --> 01:22:32.510
right now ready to tap in the combination.

1274
01:22:32.510 --> 01:22:33.710
Give me the first six numbers

1275
01:22:33.710 --> 01:22:35.430
that come to your head right now.

1276
01:22:35.430 --> 01:22:36.270
I have no idea.

1277
01:22:36.270 --> 01:22:37.910
Right now!

1278
01:22:37.910 --> 01:22:39.390
I said right now!

1279
01:22:39.390 --> 01:22:40.230
Right now!

1280
01:22:40.230 --> 01:22:44.270
Five, two, eight, four, nine, one.

1281
01:22:47.920 --> 01:22:49.920
You have to do better than that.

1282
01:22:49.920 --> 01:22:51.240
All right, bag him.

1283
01:22:52.560 --> 01:22:53.840
We're going for a ride.

1284
01:22:57.810 --> 01:22:59.210
Worth more to your life.

1285
01:23:00.490 --> 01:23:07.370
You hear me?

1286
01:23:07.370 --> 01:23:08.210
Forget.

1287
01:23:09.210 --> 01:23:10.450
That boy's relationship with his father

1288
01:23:10.450 --> 01:23:11.730
is even worse than we imagined.

1289
01:23:11.730 --> 01:23:12.850
This helps us how?

1290
01:23:12.850 --> 01:23:13.690
The stronger the issues,

1291
01:23:13.690 --> 01:23:17.430
the more powerful the catharsis.

1292
01:23:17.430 --> 01:23:18.710
How are you gonna reconcile them

1293
01:23:18.710 --> 01:23:19.550
if they're so estranged?

1294
01:23:19.550 --> 01:23:20.630
Well, I'm working on that, aren't I?

1295
01:23:20.630 --> 01:23:21.910
You look fast.

1296
01:23:21.910 --> 01:23:24.310
Projections are closing in quick.

1297
01:23:24.310 --> 01:23:25.590
We gotta break out of here

1298
01:23:25.590 --> 01:24:03.980
before we're totally boxed in.

1299
01:24:03.980 --> 01:24:06.420
You mustn't be afraid to dream a little bigger, darling.

1300
01:24:06.420 --> 01:24:26.620
You shift his animosity from his father to his godfather.

1301
01:24:26.620 --> 01:24:28.620
You're gonna destroy his one positive relationship?

1302
01:24:28.620 --> 01:24:30.820
No, we repair his relationship with his father

1303
01:24:30.820 --> 01:24:33.740
by exposing his godfather's true nature.

1304
01:24:33.780 --> 01:24:35.300
We should charge Fisher a lot more than science

1305
01:24:35.300 --> 01:24:36.860
over this job.

1306
01:24:36.860 --> 01:24:37.820
What about his security?

1307
01:24:37.820 --> 01:24:39.540
It's gonna get worse as we go deeper.

1308
01:24:39.540 --> 01:24:41.700
I think we run with Mr. Charles.

1309
01:24:41.700 --> 01:24:42.540
No.

1310
01:24:42.540 --> 01:24:43.380
Who's Mr. Charles?

1311
01:24:43.380 --> 01:24:44.220
Bad idea.

1312
01:24:44.220 --> 01:24:45.460
The second we get into that hotel

1313
01:24:45.460 --> 01:24:46.420
and approach Fisher,

1314
01:24:46.420 --> 01:24:47.940
his security's gonna be all over us.

1315
01:24:47.940 --> 01:24:50.140
We run with Mr. Charles like we did on the Stein job.

1316
01:24:50.140 --> 01:24:51.100
So you've done it before?

1317
01:24:51.100 --> 01:24:52.540
Yeah, and it didn't work.

1318
01:24:52.540 --> 01:24:54.020
The subject realized he was dreaming

1319
01:24:54.020 --> 01:24:55.900
and his subconscious tore us to pieces.

1320
01:24:55.900 --> 01:24:57.940
Excellent, but you learned a lot, right?

1321
01:24:57.940 --> 01:24:59.300
I need some kind of distraction.

1322
01:24:59.300 --> 01:25:00.420
No problem.

1323
01:25:00.420 --> 01:25:02.900
How about a lovely lady that I've used before?

1324
01:25:02.900 --> 01:25:04.860
Listen to me, you drive carefully, all right?

1325
01:25:04.860 --> 01:25:12.050
Everything down there is gonna be unstable as hell.

1326
01:25:12.050 --> 01:25:13.610
Don't jump too soon.

1327
01:25:13.610 --> 01:25:15.570
We only got one shot at that cake we gotta make.

1328
01:25:15.570 --> 01:25:16.970
I'll play the music to let you know it's coming.

1329
01:25:16.970 --> 01:25:18.010
The rest is on you.

1330
01:25:19.050 --> 01:25:19.890
You ready?

1331
01:25:19.890 --> 01:25:22.330
Ready!

1332
01:25:22.330 --> 01:25:23.690
Sweet dreams.

1333
01:25:23.690 --> 01:25:26.660
Am I boring you?

1334
01:25:26.660 --> 01:25:28.540
I was telling you my story.

1335
01:25:28.540 --> 01:25:35.900
I guess it wasn't to your liking.

1336
01:25:35.900 --> 01:25:43.010
There goes Mr. Charles.

1337
01:25:43.010 --> 01:25:45.250
Fisher, right?

1338
01:25:45.250 --> 01:25:47.850
Pleasure to see you again, Rod Green from marketing.

1339
01:25:48.810 --> 01:25:51.330
Hm, and you must be?

1340
01:25:51.330 --> 01:26:02.400
Leaving, in case you get bored.

1341
01:26:02.400 --> 01:26:03.840
Must have blown you off.

1342
01:26:03.840 --> 01:26:05.080
That is unless her phone number

1343
01:26:05.080 --> 01:26:06.960
really is only six digits.

1344
01:26:06.960 --> 01:26:10.200
Funny way to make friends,

1345
01:26:10.200 --> 01:26:12.680
someone stealing your wallet like that.

1346
01:26:12.680 --> 01:26:19.120
The loan's worth at least $500.

1347
01:26:19.120 --> 01:26:20.720
About $500, right?

1348
01:26:20.720 --> 01:26:21.640
Listen, don't worry about it.

1349
01:26:21.640 --> 01:26:24.000
My people are already on it as we speak.

1350
01:26:24.000 --> 01:26:26.080
Who or what is Mr. Charles?

1351
01:26:26.080 --> 01:26:27.680
It's a gambit designed to turn Fisher

1352
01:26:27.680 --> 01:26:29.280
against his own subconscious.

1353
01:26:30.160 --> 01:26:31.400
And why don't you approve?

1354
01:26:31.400 --> 01:26:33.520
Because it involves telling the Mark that he's dreaming,

1355
01:26:33.560 --> 01:26:36.120
which involves attracting a lot of attention to us.

1356
01:26:36.120 --> 01:26:38.000
Didn't Cobb say anything to do that?

1357
01:26:38.000 --> 01:26:40.360
Hm, so now you've noticed how much time

1358
01:26:40.360 --> 01:26:43.040
Cobb spends doing things he says never to do.

1359
01:26:43.040 --> 01:26:47.630
Mr. Sire, can I have a moment?

1360
01:26:47.630 --> 01:26:48.470
I'm sorry about the plan.

1361
01:26:48.470 --> 01:26:51.100
No, wait!

1362
01:26:51.100 --> 01:26:52.540
You look a bit back, yeah?

1363
01:26:52.540 --> 01:26:54.540
Very amusing, Mr. Eames.

1364
01:26:54.540 --> 01:27:02.980
It's on the plan.

1365
01:27:02.980 --> 01:27:04.900
No, it's much closer.

1366
01:27:04.900 --> 01:27:15.100
It's useless driving.

1367
01:27:15.100 --> 01:27:17.460
I'm sorry, who did you say you were?

1368
01:27:17.460 --> 01:27:18.820
Rod Green from marketing.

1369
01:27:19.900 --> 01:27:21.540
That's not true at all, is it?

1370
01:27:21.540 --> 01:27:29.100
Security down here.

1371
01:27:30.180 --> 01:27:32.420
Get out on a different floor, keep moving.

1372
01:27:32.420 --> 01:27:35.220
Dump the wallet, security, we're looking for that.

1373
01:27:35.220 --> 01:27:36.060
Okay.

1374
01:27:36.060 --> 01:27:42.100
We need to buy Cobb a little more time.

1375
01:27:42.100 --> 01:27:46.060
Security, huh?

1376
01:27:46.060 --> 01:27:47.100
You work for the hotel?

1377
01:27:47.100 --> 01:27:48.380
No, no.

1378
01:27:48.380 --> 01:27:52.020
I specialize in a very specific type of security.

1379
01:27:53.420 --> 01:27:55.180
Subconscious security.

1380
01:27:55.180 --> 01:27:56.540
You talking about dreams?

1381
01:27:57.540 --> 01:28:00.580
You talking about extraction?

1382
01:28:00.580 --> 01:28:17.860
Fisher, I'm here to protect you

1383
01:28:17.860 --> 01:28:20.980
in the event that someone tries to access your mind

1384
01:28:20.980 --> 01:28:27.290
through your dreams, you're not safe here before you.

1385
01:28:46.030 --> 01:28:52.990
Strange weather, isn't it?

1386
01:28:52.990 --> 01:28:56.100
You feel that?

1387
01:28:56.100 --> 01:28:57.340
What's happening?

1388
01:28:57.340 --> 01:28:58.660
Cobb's drawing Fisher's attention

1389
01:28:58.660 --> 01:29:00.540
to the strangeness of the dream,

1390
01:29:00.540 --> 01:29:03.700
which is making his subconscious look for the dreamer.

1391
01:29:03.700 --> 01:29:04.740
For me.

1392
01:29:04.740 --> 01:29:11.810
Quick, give me a kiss.

1393
01:29:11.810 --> 01:29:13.770
They're still looking at us?

1394
01:29:13.770 --> 01:29:15.130
Yeah, it's worth a shot.

1395
01:29:16.410 --> 01:29:26.620
We should probably get out of here.

1396
01:29:33.700 --> 01:29:35.340
You feel that?

1397
01:29:35.340 --> 01:29:37.340
You've actually been trained for this, Mr. Fisher.

1398
01:29:37.340 --> 01:29:39.900
Pay attention to the strangeness of the weather,

1399
01:29:39.900 --> 01:29:41.740
the shift in gravity.

1400
01:29:41.740 --> 01:29:42.900
None of this is real.

1401
01:29:43.860 --> 01:29:44.940
You're in a dream.

1402
01:29:44.940 --> 01:29:51.570
The easiest way for you to test yourself

1403
01:29:51.570 --> 01:29:54.410
is to try and remember how you arrived at this hotel.

1404
01:29:54.410 --> 01:29:55.330
Can you do that?

1405
01:29:56.810 --> 01:30:18.140
Yeah, I got affection of your subconscious.

1406
01:30:18.140 --> 01:30:19.420
I was sent here to protect you

1407
01:30:19.420 --> 01:30:21.380
in the event that extractors tried to pull you

1408
01:30:21.380 --> 01:30:24.820
into a dream, and I believe that's what's going on

1409
01:30:24.820 --> 01:31:04.970
right now, Mr. Fisher.

1410
01:31:05.010 --> 01:31:09.750
If you want my help, you have to remain calm.

1411
01:31:09.750 --> 01:31:27.620
I need you to work with me, Mr. Fisher.

1412
01:31:27.620 --> 01:31:29.620
I wouldn't do that if I were you, Mr. Fisher.

1413
01:31:29.620 --> 01:31:30.940
I believe they have you sedated,

1414
01:31:30.940 --> 01:31:34.460
and if you pull that trigger, you may not wake up.

1415
01:31:35.660 --> 01:31:37.340
You may go into a further dream state.

1416
01:31:37.340 --> 01:32:00.070
Now, you know what I'm talking about.

1417
01:32:00.070 --> 01:32:02.350
This room should be directly below 528.

1418
01:32:02.350 --> 01:32:12.350
Yeah.

1419
01:32:12.350 --> 01:32:13.830
Think, Mr. Fisher, think.

1420
01:32:13.830 --> 01:32:17.030
What do you remember from before this dream?

1421
01:32:17.030 --> 01:32:20.670
Oh, there was a lot of gunfire.

1422
01:32:20.670 --> 01:32:26.540
There was rain.

1423
01:32:26.540 --> 01:32:27.780
We'd been kidnapped.

1424
01:32:27.780 --> 01:32:32.760
Where were they holding me?

1425
01:32:32.760 --> 01:32:34.080
They had us in the back of a van.

1426
01:32:34.080 --> 01:32:36.160
That explains the gravity shifts.

1427
01:32:36.160 --> 01:32:37.480
You're in the back of a van right now.

1428
01:32:37.480 --> 01:32:38.400
Keep going.

1429
01:32:38.400 --> 01:32:43.400
It had something to do with a safe.

1430
01:32:44.840 --> 01:32:46.280
God, why is it so hard to remember?

1431
01:32:46.280 --> 01:32:47.960
It's like trying to remember a dream

1432
01:32:47.960 --> 01:32:49.760
after you've woken up, isn't it?

1433
01:32:49.760 --> 01:32:51.720
It takes years of practice.

1434
01:32:51.760 --> 01:32:54.200
You and Browning have been pulled into this dream

1435
01:32:54.200 --> 01:32:56.520
because they're trying to steal something from your mind.

1436
01:32:56.520 --> 01:33:00.560
I need you to focus and try and remember what that is.

1437
01:33:00.560 --> 01:33:02.080
What is it, Mr. Fisher, think!

1438
01:33:02.080 --> 01:33:03.920
Oh, a combination.

1439
01:33:03.920 --> 01:33:06.600
They demanded the first numbers to pop into my head.

1440
01:33:06.600 --> 01:33:09.240
They're trying to extract a number from your subconscious.

1441
01:33:09.240 --> 01:33:10.600
It can represent anything.

1442
01:33:10.600 --> 01:33:13.860
We're in a hotel right now.

1443
01:33:13.860 --> 01:33:15.900
We should try hotel rooms.

1444
01:33:15.900 --> 01:33:17.060
What was the number, Mr. Fisher?

1445
01:33:17.060 --> 01:33:18.100
Try and remember for me.

1446
01:33:18.100 --> 01:33:20.020
This is very important.

1447
01:33:20.020 --> 01:33:20.860
Five.

1448
01:33:21.860 --> 01:33:23.860
Five, two, it was something.

1449
01:33:23.860 --> 01:33:24.700
It was a long number.

1450
01:33:24.700 --> 01:33:25.540
That's good enough.

1451
01:33:25.540 --> 01:33:26.380
We can start there.

1452
01:33:26.380 --> 01:33:27.220
Fifth floor.

1453
01:33:27.220 --> 01:33:28.380
Yep.

1454
01:33:28.380 --> 01:33:30.020
So do you use a timer?

1455
01:33:30.020 --> 01:33:32.660
No, I have to judge it for myself.

1456
01:33:32.660 --> 01:33:34.860
While you're all asleep in five, two, eight,

1457
01:33:34.860 --> 01:33:36.260
I wait for Yasuf's kick.

1458
01:33:36.260 --> 01:33:37.180
Well, how will you know?

1459
01:33:37.180 --> 01:33:38.260
His music warns me.

1460
01:33:38.260 --> 01:33:40.620
And then when the van hits the barrier of the bridge,

1461
01:33:40.620 --> 01:33:42.220
that should be unmistakable.

1462
01:33:42.220 --> 01:33:45.900
So we get a nice synchronized kick.

1463
01:33:45.900 --> 01:33:48.460
If it's too soon, we won't get pulled out.

1464
01:33:48.460 --> 01:33:51.700
If it's too late, we won't be able to drop this.

1465
01:33:51.700 --> 01:33:52.740
Well, why not?

1466
01:33:52.740 --> 01:33:56.260
Because the van will be in free fall.

1467
01:33:56.260 --> 01:33:58.260
Can't drop you without gravity.

1468
01:33:58.260 --> 01:34:04.490
Right.

1469
01:34:04.490 --> 01:34:31.380
With me.

1470
01:34:31.380 --> 01:34:32.460
Mr. Charles.

1471
01:34:32.460 --> 01:34:34.020
Do you know what that is, Mr. Fisher?

1472
01:34:34.020 --> 01:34:35.540
Yeah, I think so, yeah.

1473
01:34:35.540 --> 01:34:38.020
They were trying to put you under.

1474
01:34:38.020 --> 01:34:39.060
I'm already under.

1475
01:34:39.060 --> 01:34:40.180
Under again.

1476
01:34:40.180 --> 01:34:43.420
What do you mean, a dream within a dream?

1477
01:34:43.420 --> 01:34:46.180
Hey, I see you changed.

1478
01:34:46.180 --> 01:34:48.680
I'm sorry?

1479
01:34:48.680 --> 01:34:49.480
I'm sorry.

1480
01:34:49.520 --> 01:34:53.820
I'm Mr. Giffalfell.

1481
01:34:53.820 --> 01:34:55.940
Good looking fella, I'm sure.

1482
01:34:55.940 --> 01:35:00.240
His projection of browning has followed him

1483
01:35:00.240 --> 01:35:01.640
to see how he behaves.

1484
01:35:01.640 --> 01:35:02.520
Why?

1485
01:35:02.520 --> 01:35:04.080
Because how he acts will tell us

1486
01:35:04.080 --> 01:35:06.120
if Fisher was starting to suspect his motives the way

1487
01:35:06.120 --> 01:35:12.910
we want him to.

1488
01:35:12.910 --> 01:35:14.150
Peter?

1489
01:35:14.150 --> 01:35:15.470
Said you were kidnapped together?

1490
01:35:15.470 --> 01:35:17.190
Well, um, well, not exactly.

1491
01:35:17.190 --> 01:35:18.270
They already had him.

1492
01:35:18.270 --> 01:35:19.150
They were torturing him.

1493
01:35:19.150 --> 01:35:20.510
And you saw them torture him.

1494
01:35:20.510 --> 01:35:33.120
Kidnappers are working for you.

1495
01:35:33.120 --> 01:35:35.200
That's safe open.

1496
01:35:35.200 --> 01:35:36.800
Is he going to do alternate will?

1497
01:35:36.800 --> 01:35:39.480
Fisher Morrow has been my entire life.

1498
01:35:39.560 --> 01:35:41.160
I can't let you destroy it.

1499
01:35:41.160 --> 01:35:42.760
I'm not going to throw away my inheritance.

1500
01:35:42.760 --> 01:35:43.720
Why would I?

1501
01:35:43.720 --> 01:35:48.600
I couldn't let you rise to your father's last taunt.

1502
01:35:48.600 --> 01:35:49.600
A taunt?

1503
01:35:49.600 --> 01:35:50.760
The will, Robert.

1504
01:35:50.760 --> 01:35:55.720
That will, that's his last insult. A challenge for you

1505
01:35:55.720 --> 01:35:57.960
to build something for yourself,

1506
01:35:57.960 --> 01:36:08.340
but telling you you're not worthy of his accomplishments.

1507
01:36:08.340 --> 01:36:11.300
That he was disappointed.

1508
01:36:11.300 --> 01:36:16.220
I'm sorry, but he's wrong.

1509
01:36:17.940 --> 01:36:20.580
You can build a better company than he ever did.

1510
01:36:20.580 --> 01:36:22.460
Mr. Fisher?

1511
01:36:22.460 --> 01:36:23.380
He's lying.

1512
01:36:23.380 --> 01:36:25.300
I mean, trust me, it's what I do.

1513
01:36:25.300 --> 01:36:29.820
He's hiding something, and we need to find out what that is.

1514
01:36:29.820 --> 01:36:31.660
I need you to do the same thing to him

1515
01:36:31.660 --> 01:36:33.460
that he was going to do to you.

1516
01:36:35.660 --> 01:36:37.420
We'll enter his subconscious and find out what

1517
01:36:37.420 --> 01:36:48.460
he doesn't want you to know.

1518
01:36:48.460 --> 01:36:49.260
He's out.

1519
01:36:49.260 --> 01:36:52.340
Wait, whose subconscious are we going into exactly?

1520
01:36:52.340 --> 01:36:53.740
We're going into Fisher's.

1521
01:36:53.740 --> 01:36:55.100
I told him it was Browning's, so he'd

1522
01:36:55.100 --> 01:36:56.500
come be a part of our team.

1523
01:36:56.500 --> 01:36:58.820
He's going to help us break into his own subconscious.

1524
01:36:58.820 --> 01:37:00.540
That's right.

1525
01:37:00.540 --> 01:37:03.060
Security's going to let me down, Browning.

1526
01:37:03.060 --> 01:37:05.860
And I will lead them on a merry chase.

1527
01:37:05.860 --> 01:37:07.300
Just be back before the kid.

1528
01:37:07.300 --> 01:37:08.860
Go to sleep, Mr. Reeves.

1529
01:37:08.860 --> 01:37:19.390
You ready?

1530
01:37:19.390 --> 01:37:21.550
Yes, yes, I'm fine.

1531
01:37:21.550 --> 01:37:35.620
I'm ready.

1532
01:37:35.620 --> 01:37:43.660
Cop, what's down there?

1533
01:37:43.660 --> 01:37:46.260
Really, the truth, we want Fisher to learn.

1534
01:37:46.260 --> 01:37:48.020
I mean, what's down there for you?

1535
01:40:48.400 --> 01:40:49.960
From the complex, you understand?

1536
01:40:49.960 --> 01:40:51.240
Who drives Fisher in?

1537
01:40:51.240 --> 01:40:52.160
Not me.

1538
01:40:52.160 --> 01:40:54.880
If I know the route, everything can be compromised.

1539
01:40:54.880 --> 01:40:56.000
I designed the place.

1540
01:40:56.320 --> 01:40:57.560
Now, you're with me.

1541
01:40:57.560 --> 01:41:00.160
I predict.

1542
01:41:00.160 --> 01:41:02.120
You brief him on the route into the complex.

1543
01:41:02.120 --> 01:41:04.080
Fisher, we'll be going with him.

1544
01:41:04.080 --> 01:41:05.000
All right.

1545
01:41:05.000 --> 01:41:05.880
What about you?

1546
01:41:05.880 --> 01:41:09.690
I'll be listening in the whole time.

1547
01:41:09.690 --> 01:41:11.570
The windows on the upper floor are big enough for me

1548
01:41:11.570 --> 01:41:12.970
to cover you from that south tower.

1549
01:41:12.970 --> 01:41:13.770
You see it?

1550
01:41:13.770 --> 01:41:14.570
Yeah.

1551
01:41:14.570 --> 01:41:15.370
You're not coming in?

1552
01:41:15.370 --> 01:41:17.170
In order to find out the truth about your father,

1553
01:41:17.170 --> 01:41:17.970
you're going to need to break

1554
01:41:17.970 --> 01:41:21.370
into Browning's mind on your own.

1555
01:41:21.370 --> 01:43:19.030
Come on, Fisher.

1556
01:43:19.030 --> 01:43:22.090
It's music.

1557
01:43:22.090 --> 01:43:23.410
Move fast.

1558
01:43:23.410 --> 01:43:33.260
This is 10 seconds from the jump, which gives

1559
01:43:33.260 --> 01:43:38.820
Arthur three minutes.

1560
01:43:38.860 --> 01:43:39.780
Which gives us what?

1561
01:43:39.780 --> 01:43:40.660
60 minutes.

1562
01:43:40.660 --> 01:43:42.220
Can they make that route in under an hour?

1563
01:43:42.220 --> 01:43:44.140
They still have to climb down to the middle terrace.

1564
01:43:44.140 --> 01:43:58.550
Well, then they need a new route, a more direct route.

1565
01:43:58.550 --> 01:44:00.030
It's designed as a labyrinth.

1566
01:44:00.030 --> 01:44:02.190
There must be access routes that cut through the maze,

1567
01:44:02.190 --> 01:44:03.110
right?

1568
01:44:03.110 --> 01:44:27.690
Eames.

1569
01:44:27.690 --> 01:44:28.850
Did Eames add any features?

1570
01:44:28.850 --> 01:44:29.930
I don't think I should tell you.

1571
01:44:29.930 --> 01:44:30.770
If Maul finds out, then-

1572
01:44:30.770 --> 01:44:31.730
We don't have time for this.

1573
01:44:31.730 --> 01:44:33.610
Did he add anything?

1574
01:44:33.610 --> 01:44:36.130
He added an air dock system that can cut through the maze.

1575
01:44:36.130 --> 01:44:37.530
Good. Explain it to them.

1576
01:44:37.530 --> 01:44:38.490
Thank you.

1577
01:44:38.490 --> 01:46:27.240
Go ahead.

1578
01:46:27.240 --> 01:46:28.520
Carl, did we miss it?

1579
01:46:28.520 --> 01:46:29.560
Yeah, we missed it.

1580
01:46:30.320 --> 01:46:31.480
Yeah.

1581
01:46:31.480 --> 01:46:32.600
Couldn't sell it.

1582
01:46:32.600 --> 01:46:35.480
I've drank up a goddamn beach.

1583
01:46:35.480 --> 01:46:40.490
Huh?

1584
01:46:40.490 --> 01:46:42.450
We finished the job before the next kick.

1585
01:46:42.450 --> 01:46:43.290
What next kick?

1586
01:46:43.290 --> 01:47:18.820
When the van hits the water.

1587
01:47:18.820 --> 01:47:20.300
Arthur has a couple minutes.

1588
01:47:20.300 --> 01:47:21.580
We have about 20.

1589
01:47:21.580 --> 01:48:06.050
Six more time, all right?

1590
01:48:06.050 --> 01:49:52.570
Is this stronger than having any windows?

1591
01:49:52.570 --> 01:49:54.170
Well, I mean, it wouldn't be very strong if it did.

1592
01:49:54.170 --> 01:49:56.210
Let's hope Fisher likes what he finds in there.

1593
01:49:56.210 --> 01:50:02.010
It's part of his subconscious.

1594
01:50:02.010 --> 01:50:03.610
Are you destroying those parts of his mind?

1595
01:50:03.610 --> 01:50:05.130
I don't know. They're just projections.

1596
01:50:05.130 --> 01:50:33.470
Clear, but hurry.

1597
01:50:33.470 --> 01:50:35.590
There's an entire army headed your way.

1598
01:50:35.590 --> 01:52:12.430
Projection.

1599
01:53:20.820 --> 01:53:21.660
Reviving him.

1600
01:53:21.660 --> 01:53:23.460
His mind's already trapped down there.

1601
01:53:23.460 --> 01:53:26.180
It's all over.

1602
01:53:26.180 --> 01:53:27.620
So that's it, then we found?

1603
01:53:27.620 --> 01:53:34.490
I'm sorry.

1604
01:53:34.490 --> 01:53:36.650
Well, it's not me that doesn't get back to my family, is it?

1605
01:53:36.650 --> 01:53:39.790
Shame. I really want to know what's going to happen in there.

1606
01:53:39.790 --> 01:53:41.990
I swear we have this one.

1607
01:53:41.990 --> 01:53:45.910
Let's set the charges.

1608
01:53:45.910 --> 01:53:48.310
No, there's still another way.

1609
01:53:48.310 --> 01:53:50.670
We just have to follow Fisher down there.

1610
01:53:50.670 --> 01:53:51.990
Not enough time.

1611
01:53:51.990 --> 01:53:55.830
No, but there will be enough time down there.

1612
01:53:55.830 --> 01:53:57.350
And we will find him, OK?

1613
01:53:57.350 --> 01:53:59.790
As soon as Arthur's music kicks in,

1614
01:53:59.790 --> 01:54:01.470
just use the defibrillator to revive him.

1615
01:54:01.470 --> 01:54:05.470
We can give him his own kick down below.

1616
01:54:05.470 --> 01:54:07.230
Look, you get him in there.

1617
01:54:07.230 --> 01:54:10.110
As soon as the music ends, you blow up the hospital,

1618
01:54:10.110 --> 01:54:14.330
and we all ride the kick back up the lairs.

1619
01:54:14.330 --> 01:54:16.290
Well, it's worth the shot.

1620
01:54:16.290 --> 01:54:19.250
If Saito can hold the guards up while I set the charges.

1621
01:54:19.250 --> 01:54:23.230
Saito will never make it, will he?

1622
01:54:23.230 --> 01:54:25.150
We've got to try this.

1623
01:54:25.150 --> 01:54:26.510
Go for it.

1624
01:54:26.510 --> 01:54:27.670
If you are not back before the kick,

1625
01:54:27.670 --> 01:54:28.870
I am gone with or without you.

1626
01:54:28.870 --> 01:54:29.870
She's right.

1627
01:54:36.780 --> 01:54:38.420
I trust you to do what needs to happen here.

1628
01:54:38.420 --> 01:54:40.300
I mean, Mal's going to be down there.

1629
01:54:40.300 --> 01:54:41.700
I know where to find her.

1630
01:54:41.700 --> 01:54:42.580
She'll have Fisher.

1631
01:54:42.580 --> 01:54:43.500
How do you know?

1632
01:54:43.500 --> 01:54:46.900
Because she wants me to come after her.

1633
01:54:46.900 --> 01:54:48.940
She wants me back down there with her.

1634
01:54:48.940 --> 01:55:25.850
You broke?

1635
01:55:25.850 --> 01:55:27.690
What?

1636
01:55:27.690 --> 01:56:23.850
This is where she'll be, to take care of Fisher

1637
01:56:23.850 --> 01:56:25.290
when I go set some charges, OK?

1638
01:56:25.290 --> 01:56:27.210
No one's room for a tourist on me.

1639
01:56:27.210 --> 01:58:07.480
Started in on the memory.

1640
01:58:07.480 --> 01:58:09.640
It was their first apartment.

1641
01:58:09.640 --> 01:58:11.960
And we moved to that building right there.

1642
01:58:11.960 --> 01:58:14.640
After Mal became pregnant, that became our home.

1643
01:58:14.640 --> 01:58:17.640
You reconstructed all of this from memory?

1644
01:58:17.640 --> 01:58:20.080
Like I told you, we had lots of time.

1645
01:58:20.080 --> 01:58:23.100
What is that?

1646
01:58:23.100 --> 01:58:24.980
It's the house Mal grew up in.

1647
01:58:24.980 --> 01:58:27.920
Will she be in there?

1648
01:58:27.920 --> 01:58:29.040
Come on.

1649
01:58:29.040 --> 01:58:30.480
We both wanted to live in a house,

1650
01:58:30.480 --> 01:58:32.080
but we love this type of building.

1651
01:58:32.080 --> 01:58:35.040
In the real world, we'd have to choose, but not here.

1652
01:58:35.040 --> 01:59:17.790
Bring Fisher back.

1653
01:59:17.790 --> 01:59:24.860
Mal put some kind of an improvise.

1654
01:59:24.860 --> 01:59:27.660
Listen, there's something you should know about me,

1655
01:59:27.660 --> 01:59:29.020
about inception.

1656
01:59:29.020 --> 01:59:48.750
An idea is like a virus, resilient, highly contagious.

1657
01:59:48.750 --> 01:59:51.950
And the smallest seed of an idea can grow.

1658
01:59:52.030 --> 01:59:57.740
Will it define or destroy you?

1659
01:59:57.740 --> 02:00:06.020
The smallest idea, such as, your world is not real.

1660
02:00:07.140 --> 02:00:12.100
Simple little thought that changes everything.

1661
02:00:12.100 --> 02:00:15.700
So certain of your world, of what's real.

1662
02:00:16.580 --> 02:00:17.540
Do you think he is?

1663
02:00:20.180 --> 02:00:22.340
Or do you think he's as lost as I was?

1664
02:00:24.180 --> 02:00:25.380
I know what's real, Mal.

1665
02:00:27.940 --> 02:00:29.620
No creeping doubts.

1666
02:00:30.500 --> 02:00:32.660
Not feeling persecuted, dumb.

1667
02:00:33.460 --> 02:00:37.700
Chased around the globe by anonymous corporations and police forces.

1668
02:00:37.700 --> 02:00:40.340
The way the projections persecute the dreamer.

1669
02:00:40.340 --> 02:00:43.040
Admit it.

1670
02:00:43.040 --> 02:00:47.040
I don't believe in one reality anymore.

1671
02:00:47.840 --> 02:00:48.960
So choose.

1672
02:00:49.760 --> 02:00:51.040
Choose to be here.

1673
02:00:52.320 --> 02:00:53.120
Choose me.

1674
02:00:53.840 --> 02:01:27.310
You're wrong.

1675
02:01:28.190 --> 02:01:28.830
Not wrong.

1676
02:01:28.830 --> 02:01:30.030
You are confused.

1677
02:01:31.870 --> 02:01:33.630
Our children are here.

1678
02:01:33.630 --> 02:01:41.090
Up above, Mal.

1679
02:01:58.260 --> 02:01:59.380
Listen to yourself.

1680
02:02:00.020 --> 02:02:01.620
These are our children.

1681
02:02:04.350 --> 02:02:05.630
James, Philippa.

1682
02:02:07.150 --> 02:02:08.990
Please, those aren't my children.

1683
02:02:08.990 --> 02:02:11.390
You keep telling yourself that, but you don't believe it.

1684
02:02:11.390 --> 02:02:12.110
No, I know it.

1685
02:02:12.110 --> 02:02:12.990
And what if you're wrong?

1686
02:02:13.550 --> 02:02:15.470
What if I'm what's real?

1687
02:02:17.070 --> 02:02:24.140
You keep telling yourself what you know, but what do you believe?

1688
02:02:24.140 --> 02:02:25.660
What do you feel?

1689
02:02:25.660 --> 02:02:38.780
Hopeless I am.

1690
02:02:38.780 --> 02:02:52.770
Guilt the idea that caused you to question your reality came from me.

1691
02:02:56.800 --> 02:02:59.440
You planted the idea in my mind.

1692
02:02:59.440 --> 02:03:02.660
What is she talking about?

1693
02:03:03.860 --> 02:03:08.500
The reason I knew Inception was possible was because I did it to her first.

1694
02:03:08.500 --> 02:03:20.060
We were lost in here and accepted.

1695
02:03:24.060 --> 02:03:25.660
She had locked something away.

1696
02:03:25.660 --> 02:03:26.460
Something.

1697
02:03:26.460 --> 02:03:33.900
The truth that she had once known, but chose to forget.

1698
02:03:40.640 --> 02:03:48.080
So I decided to search for her in the recess of her mind and found that secret place.

1699
02:03:48.960 --> 02:03:57.650
Night broke in, an idea, everything.

1700
02:03:57.650 --> 02:04:05.150
Her world wasn't real.

1701
02:04:05.150 --> 02:04:30.460
Waiting for a train.

1702
02:04:30.460 --> 02:04:34.830
You're far away.

1703
02:04:37.120 --> 02:04:42.430
You know where you hope this train will take you, but you can't know for sure.

1704
02:04:44.350 --> 02:04:45.390
And it doesn't matter.

1705
02:04:47.310 --> 02:04:48.590
Now tell me why.

1706
02:04:48.590 --> 02:04:50.750
Because you did it together.

1707
02:04:50.750 --> 02:04:59.200
That idea would grow in her mind like a cancer.

1708
02:04:59.200 --> 02:05:20.210
That even after she woke, the world wasn't real on the escape.

1709
02:05:20.210 --> 02:05:21.250
Jesus.

1710
02:05:21.330 --> 02:05:23.490
You're infecting my mind.

1711
02:05:23.490 --> 02:05:24.770
I was trying to save you.

1712
02:05:24.770 --> 02:05:25.890
You betrayed me.

1713
02:05:27.170 --> 02:05:28.770
But you can make amends.

1714
02:05:28.770 --> 02:05:30.850
You can still keep your promise.

1715
02:05:30.850 --> 02:05:36.450
We can still be together right here in the world we built together.

1716
02:05:36.450 --> 02:07:11.760
Fisher's on the path.

1717
02:07:11.760 --> 02:07:15.900
I can't do this.

1718
02:07:15.900 --> 02:07:17.660
Go check he's alive right now.

1719
02:07:17.660 --> 02:07:18.160
Do it.

1720
02:07:37.730 --> 02:07:39.250
Take Fisher with you, all right?

1721
02:07:39.250 --> 02:07:41.170
You can't stay here to be with her.

1722
02:07:43.860 --> 02:07:44.360
I'm not.

1723
02:07:45.300 --> 02:07:46.500
Saito's dead by now.

1724
02:07:46.500 --> 02:07:48.500
That means he's down here somewhere.

1725
02:07:48.500 --> 02:07:52.160
That means I have to find him.

1726
02:07:52.160 --> 02:07:54.880
I can't stay with her anymore because she doesn't exist.

1727
02:07:55.520 --> 02:07:56.960
I'm the only thing you do.

1728
02:07:56.960 --> 02:08:23.150
It's a shade of my real life.

1729
02:08:24.190 --> 02:08:29.620
You remember the best that I can do, but you're just not good enough.

1730
02:08:34.370 --> 02:08:35.090
What are you doing?

1731
02:08:36.290 --> 02:08:36.850
Improvise.

1732
02:08:49.140 --> 02:08:49.940
Go, go, go, go.

1733
02:09:58.320 --> 02:14:54.030
Just to live for him.

1734
02:14:54.030 --> 02:15:11.100
That's what I'm gonna do, Uncle Peter.

1735
02:15:11.100 --> 02:15:11.900
With Ma?

1736
02:15:11.900 --> 02:15:13.260
Not a fine sider.

1737
02:15:13.260 --> 02:15:16.290
He'll be lost.

1738
02:15:19.840 --> 02:15:20.640
No, he'll be all right.

